var textForPages =["To request updates to this document, please \u000d\u000asend an email to: nntraining@gmr.net\u000d\u000a911 Nurse Navigation \u000d\u000aJob Training & Reference Materials\u000d\u000aLast Updated: October 2, 2026\u000d\u000aPolicies & Guidelines About GMR Contracts Quick Links\u000d\u000aWorkflows System Applications Recognition","Page 2\u000d\u000aPolicies & Guidelines\u000d\u000aIn This Section\u000d\u000aThe ICC People Policies contained in this section serve as a guide to \u000d\u000aour culture, operational practices, and general workplace \u000d\u000aexpectations. You will also find 911 Nurse Navigation-specific policies \u000d\u000aand procedures outlined here. For a complete list of all GMR \u000d\u000apolicies, including the Code of Conduct, please visit the GMR People \u000d\u000aServices GPS Portal.","Reference Topics\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 3\u000d\u000aNew Hire Attestation Form\u000d\u000aAttendance Policy\u000d\u000aBreaks & Shift Relief\u000d\u000aPaid Time Off\u000d\u000aShift Swaps & Giveaways\u000d\u000aJob Preparedness & Shift Restrictions\u000d\u000aDistractions\u000d\u000aAppearance\u000d\u000aCompany-Issued ID Badge\u000d\u000aLockers & Personal Belongings\u000d\u000aCondition & Upkeep of Facilities\u000d\u000aTobacco & Smoke-Free Workplace\u000d\u000aPhoenix: Tobacco & Electronic Cigarettes\u000d\u000aInclement Weather\u000d\u000aLactation Accommodation \u000d\u000aRespect in the Workplace\u000d\u000aContracts, Territories, & Licensing","New Hire Attestation Form\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 4\u000d\u000a \u000d\u000aAs part of your onboarding journey at Global Medical Resource (GMR), all hired employees \u000d\u000aMUST attest to their review and understanding of the policies in this section. Complete your \u000d\u000aattestation by submitting the following form:\u000d\u000a\ud83d\udd17100-ICC People Policies Attestation_NN\u000d\u000aCompliance Consideration\u000d\u000aIn addition to the policies herein, you are required to complete mandatory compliance \u000d\u000atraining on a yearly basis, for more information, please reach out to your trainer or \u000d\u000asupervisor. \u000d\u000aView your pending learning assignments and transcripts on \ud83d\udd17CornerStone.","Attendance Policy\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 5\u000d\u000aPolicy Number: 100-01 Subject: Attendance \u000d\u000aRevision Date: January 8th, 2026 Effective Date: January 8th, 2026\u000d\u000aI. PURPOSE \u000d\u000aTo establish expectations that employees report to work for all scheduled hours, including \u000d\u000aregular shifts, assigned overtime, shift swaps, giveaways, as well as mandatory meetings and \u000d\u000aclasses. \u000d\u000aII. POLICY\u000d\u000aExpectations \u000d\u000a\u2022 Employees are expected to arrive early enough to be performing assigned duties at \u000d\u000athe start of their shift and remain until its scheduled end time without extending \u000d\u000aallotted break periods. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Employees may clock in no more than 10 minutes before their shift begins. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Employees are required to be physically present in the ICC when clocking in unless \u000d\u000athey are attending a course, meeting or other business-related obligation located \u000d\u000aoffsite. \u000d\u000aIII.PROCEDURE \u000d\u000aIf an employee is unable to meet the above expectations, the subsequent guidelines should \u000d\u000abe followed. \u000d\u000aNotification Procedure \u000d\u000a1. Employees who will be absent or anticipate being late are expected to call the \u000d\u000aCommunications Center and speak with the on-duty leader on a recorded line. \u000d\u000ao Employees are expected to call as soon as they know they will not be reporting \u000d\u000afor duty at the start of their shift. \u000d\u000a2. In the event an employee needs an extended break, to leave early or requires any other \u000d\u000ashift modification, they must speak with the on-duty leader in person.","Policies 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 6\u000d\u000ao If an on-duty leader is not present in the ICC, the employee must attempt to \u000d\u000acontact the on-duty leader and receive acknowledgement of their schedule \u000d\u000amodification. Should the employee be unable to reach their on-duty leader, the \u000d\u000amatter should be escalated to another departmental ICC on-duty leader. \u000d\u000aAttendance Record Documentation \u000d\u000a\u2022 Attendance records are kept using a rolling twelve (12) month period, calculating \u000d\u000aattendance occurrences over the previous 365 days. Occurrences are archived and \u000d\u000adeducted from the employee\u2019s record 365 days after they occur. \u000d\u000a\u2022 The highest level of corrective action taken during the merit period (January 1st \u2013\u000d\u000aDecember 31st) will be included in an employee\u2019s annual review, regardless of the \u000d\u000atotal number of occurrences on record at the conclusion of the calendar year. \u000d\u000aAppeal Process \u000d\u000a1. Employees who wish to contest an occurrence must do so via email to the \u000d\u000aCommunications Manager within thirty (30) calendar days of the date of the occurrence \u000d\u000ain question. \u000d\u000a2. Employees will receive a response to their appeal via email within ten (10) business \u000d\u000adays. Appeals that are not submitted as specified above, or those denied by the \u000d\u000aManager, will become a permanent part of the employee\u2019s attendance record. \u000d\u000aPTO Application \u000d\u000a\u2022 PTO will be applied to all absences from an employee\u2019s regularly scheduled shift, \u000d\u000aincluding those documented as FMLA. \u000d\u000a\u2022 PTO will be applied to any partial shift absence (late arrival or early departure) in \u000d\u000aone-hour increments, except in the case of Voluntary Time Off (VTO). \u000d\u000a\u2022 PTO will not be applied to absences on overtime shifts (scheduled in addition to an \u000d\u000aemployee\u2019s regular schedule). ","Policies 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 7\u000d\u000aTypes of Absences \u000d\u000a\u2022 Approved Absences - Absences arranged and authorized in advance. They may \u000d\u000ainclude: \u000d\u000ao Company observed holidays (for specified employees). \u000d\u000ao Pre-approved PTO, shift swaps, shift giveaways and scheduled shift \u000d\u000amodifications documented in the Company-approved scheduling system. \u000d\u000ao Family Medical Leave (if stated at the time of notification with an approved \u000d\u000aFMLA case). \u000d\u000a\u25aa Additionally, employees are required to notify GMR\u2019s third-party leave \u000d\u000amanagement company, in accordance with their established \u000d\u000aguidelines, of any shift, full or partial, that is missed for which FMLA \u000d\u000ahas been claimed. \u000d\u000a\u25aa Time that is not submitted to or has been denied by GMR\u2019s third-party \u000d\u000aleave management company will result in the occurrence being issued \u000d\u000aaccording to this policy. \u000d\u000ao Approved Disability Leave. \u000d\u000ao Absences related to an on-the-job injury, wherein the injury has been \u000d\u000areported to leadership, and a claim has been filed with and approved by \u000d\u000aGMR\u2019s third-party risk management company.\u000d\u000ao Bereavement per GMR policy with proper documentation. \u000d\u000ao Military Leave with proper documentation. \u000d\u000ao Jury Duty with proper documentation. \u000d\u000ao Work-related court appearances with proper documentation. \u000d\u000ao Any additional absence permitted under applicable law. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Unapproved Absences - Absences not classified as \u201capproved absences\u201d in this \u000d\u000apolicy. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Multiple Day Absences - A subsequent unapproved absence on a consecutive \u000d\u000acalendar day will be recorded as one-half of an occurrence. \u000d\u000ao Unapproved absences spanning three (3) or more consecutive calendar days \u000d\u000awill result in one (1) occurrence being recorded for each shift missed after the \u000d\u000ainitial two (2) absences. ","Policies 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 8\u000d\u000aAbsence Exceptions \u000d\u000a\u2022 Return to work with a provider note: Should an employee return to work with an \u000d\u000aofficial signed document bearing the signature of a licensed medical provider, \u000d\u000aabsences of greater than one (1) shift may be considered one (1) occurrence. \u000d\u000aDocumentation must be provided to leadership upon the employee\u2019s return to work. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Return to work following hospitalization: Absences during a hospital admission will \u000d\u000abe recorded as zero occurrences if valid paperwork inclusive of date of admission, \u000d\u000adischarge and a return-to-work date are provided to leadership upon the employee\u2019s \u000d\u000areturn to work. \u000d\u000aDocumentation \u000d\u000a\u2022 Be advised that any documentation provided to leadership for the purpose of this \u000d\u000apolicy is subject to verification, and any instance of falsification of documents may \u000d\u000aresult in corrective action, up to and including termination. \u000d\u000aDefinitions \u000d\u000a\u2022 Tardy: Reporting for duty one to ten (1-10) minutes after the scheduled start time of \u000d\u000aan employee\u2019s shift. Employees will be issued one-quarter of an occurrence. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Late: Reporting for duty more than 10 minutes after the scheduled start time but not \u000d\u000aexceeding 25% of the employee\u2019s shift duration. Employees will be issued one-half of \u000d\u000aan occurrence. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Early Departure: Leaving assigned duty prior to the scheduled end time of an \u000d\u000aemployee\u2019s shift. \u000d\u000ao Employees who work less than 75% of their scheduled shift and leave early \u000d\u000awill be issued one occurrence. \u000d\u000ao Employees who worked more than 75% of their scheduled shift and leave \u000d\u000aearly will be issued one-half of an occurrence. \u000d\u000ao Notification of early departure is to be made directly to the on-duty leader, \u000d\u000aand the employee must confirm receipt of the notification. If proper \u000d\u000anotification procedures are not followed, this may be considered job \u000d\u000aabandonment and may result in corrective action, up to and including \u000d\u000atermination.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Voluntary Time Off (VTO): Unpaid time off during periods of low demand, as \u000d\u000adetermined by an on-duty leader.","Policies 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 9\u000d\u000a\u2022 No Call / No Show: Not reporting to work within two hours of a scheduled shift \u000d\u000awithout proper notification to an on-duty leader, provided extraordinary \u000d\u000acircumstances do not apply.\u000d\u000aMultiple Occurrences (same shift)\u000d\u000aShould an employee incur a tardy or late arrival in combination with an early departure \u000d\u000aduring the same scheduled shift, each instance will be documented individually; however, \u000d\u000ano more than one occurrence will be issued. \u000d\u000aMandatory Meetings and Classes \u000d\u000aRequired meetings in addition to mandatory training or classes are considered part of an \u000d\u000aemployee's work schedule. Failure to attend these events will be recorded as an occurrence. \u000d\u000aOccurrences of Significant Impact \u000d\u000aCertain types of absences may have significant adverse effects on staffing plans. Such \u000d\u000ainstances are particularly detrimental to operational efficiency and will result in an \u000d\u000aexpedited corrective action process. The initial instance of any of the following occurrences \u000d\u000awill result in a final warning. A subsequent instance (any combination) of the occurrences \u000d\u000alisted below within a rolling 365-day period will be grounds for termination. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Calling out on a company-observed holiday. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Calling out for a scheduled shift for which PTO had been requested and denied. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Calling out unable to report to work due to inclement weather after \u000d\u000aaccommodations have been offered by the Company. \u000d\u000a\u2022 No Call / No Show \u000d\u000aProgressive Discipline \u000d\u000aExcessive occurrence accumulation will lead to progressive discipline. \"Excessive\" is defined \u000d\u000aby the following criteria: \u000d\u000a\u2022 3 \u2013 Attendance Notification \u000d\u000a\u2022 4 \u2013 Verbal Warning \u000d\u000a\u2022 5 \u2013 Written Warning \u000d\u000a\u2022 7 \u2013 Final Warning \u000d\u000a\u2022 9 \u2013 Termination ","Policies 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 10\u000d\u000aRedemptions \u000d\u000aEmployees may earn the opportunity to have occurrences removed from their attendance \u000d\u000arecord as follows:\u000d\u000a\u2022 An employee who accepts a last-minute shift coverage request from a departmental \u000d\u000aleader may have up to one full occurrence removed from their attendance record to \u000d\u000aa maximum of one per calendar quarter.\u000d\u000ao Coverage of one full shift removes one occurrence. \u000d\u000ao Coverage of a half shift removes one-half of an occurrence. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Shift redemptions will be forfeited if: \u000d\u000ao The employee has previously been offered and declined an on-call or \u000d\u000aovertime opportunity for the date in question. (Failure to respond to an \u000d\u000aovertime offer will be considered declination.) \u000d\u000ao The employees does not work all of their scheduled shifts within that pay \u000d\u000aperiod. \u000d\u000aEmployees may not have a negative attendance occurrence balance. ","Breaks & Shift Relief\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 11\u000d\u000aPolicy Number: 100-02 Subject: Breaks and Shift Relief\u000d\u000aRevision Date: January 8th, 2026 Effective Date: January 8th, 2026\u000d\u000aI. PURPOSE\u000d\u000aTo establish standards for breaks as well as proper shift relief for all GMR ICC employees. \u000d\u000aII. POLICY\u000d\u000aBreaks \u000d\u000aThis basic outline establishes typical break periods for employees based on their total shift \u000d\u000atime. Due to variable demands in our workplace, these breaks are provided on paid \u000d\u000acompany time to allow for necessary flexibility in managing fluctuating workloads.\u000d\u000aEmployees may be allotted breaks as outlined in the following chart. The specific duration \u000d\u000aand scheduling of breaks will be determined by operational leadership. \u000d\u000aTotal Shift Hours Total Break Time\u000d\u000a6 Hours 20 Minutes\u000d\u000a8 Hours 40 Minutes\u000d\u000a10+ Hours 60 Minutes\u000d\u000aWhile we make every effort to provide breaks as outlined in this policy, they are not \u000d\u000aguaranteed and are contingent upon staffing, workload and operational needs of the \u000d\u000adepartment. Additional break expectations are as follows:\u000d\u000a\u2022 Employees are expected to remain logged into their workstations and all software, as \u000d\u000awell as to utilize the designated telephone status codes appropriately during break \u000d\u000aperiods. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Employees must remain on-site and be reachable by telephone during break periods, \u000d\u000aable to return to the ICC immediately if needed. \u000d\u000a\u2022 In the rare case that there is a need to leave the premises during a break, direct \u000d\u000aacknowledgment and approval from the on-duty leader must be obtained. \u000d\u000aEmployees should clock out before leaving and clock in upon return. ","Policies 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 12\u000d\u000a\u2022 Employees are required to obtain direct acknowledgment and approval from the onduty leader before leaving the room, except during regularly scheduled breaks. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Trainees and trainers are required to take their breaks together, unless otherwise \u000d\u000ainstructed to stagger them by the on-duty leader. \u000d\u000aShift Relief\u000d\u000aTo ensure continuous operational oversight, employees should remain logged in and \u000d\u000aavailable at their workstations until properly relieved by the on-coming employee taking \u000d\u000aover their assignment.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Employees must receive the approval of the on-duty leader to end their shift if their \u000d\u000ascheduled relief is not present at the conclusion of their shift. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Air employees without proper relief may be held over for up to six (6) hours. ","Paid Time Off (PTO)\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 13\u000d\u000aPolicy Number: 100-03 Subject: Paid Time Off (PTO)\u000d\u000aRevision Date: January 8th, 2026 Effective Date: January 8th, 2026\u000d\u000aI. PURPOSE\u000d\u000aThis policy outlines procedures for requesting and approving Paid Time Off (PTO). It does not \u000d\u000agovern absences protected by federal, state, or local law, including but not limited to FMLA, \u000d\u000amilitary leave, jury duty, disability-related leave, or pregnancy-related leave. \u000d\u000aII. POLICY\u000d\u000aPTO Requests\u000d\u000a\u2022 Should be submitted via the company-approved scheduling system and \u000d\u000adepartmental process for approval. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Will be reviewed on a first requested-first considered basis. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Will be limited by departmental guidelines for staffing. \u000d\u000a\u2022 May be submitted for consideration up to 90 days prior to the intended date(s). \u000d\u000a\u2022 Must be submitted at least 30 days prior to the intended date(s). \u000d\u000ao Requests made less than 30 days in advance will be denied unless the \u000d\u000arequestor arranges shift coverage as outlined in the Shift Swaps and \u000d\u000aGiveaways Policy. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Will be reviewed by a member of leadership and a response will be provided within \u000d\u000aten (10) business days of submission when submitted per policy. \u000d\u000ao Responses will be designated as approved, denied or pending. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Will be denied if the requestor will not have sufficient PTO hours to cover the \u000d\u000aintended date(s). \u000d\u000a\u2022 For which the requestor\u2019s PTO balance is insufficient at the time of submission will \u000d\u000aremain in a pending status until the proper number of hours have accrued to cover \u000d\u000athe intended date(s). \u000d\u000a\u2022 That have been previously approved are subject to the approval being withdrawn if \u000d\u000athe requestor\u2019s PTO balance becomes insufficient for the intended date(s). The \u000d\u000aemployee will then remain responsible for their originally scheduled shift(s).\u000d\u000ao Employees may not take unpaid time off.","Policies 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 14\u000d\u000a\u2022 For Company-observed holidays will be reviewed with consideration for past holiday \u000d\u000ausage.\u000d\u000aLeadership will review all employee requests for PTO and make every effort to \u000d\u000aaccommodate eligible requests. However, requests may be denied due to operational \u000d\u000arequirements, staffing levels, or other business considerations. \u000d\u000aIt is the responsibility of the employee to confirm approval for all requested PTO date(s). \u000d\u000aShould an employee be absent without approval, corrective action per attendance standards \u000d\u000amay apply. ","Shift Swaps & Giveaways\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 15\u000d\u000aPolicy Number: 100-04 Subject: Shift Swaps & Giveaways\u000d\u000aRevision Date: January 8th, 2026 Effective Date: January 8th, 2026\u000d\u000aI. PURPOSE\u000d\u000aThis policy outlines procedures for employees to swap or give away shifts. It does not govern \u000d\u000aabsences protected by federal, state, or local law, including but not limited to FMLA, military \u000d\u000aleave, jury duty, disability-related leave, or pregnancy-related leave.\u000d\u000aII. POLICY\u000d\u000aShift Swaps \u000d\u000aEmployees are eligible to swap shifts if: \u000d\u000a\u2022 They have been fully cleared from training. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Both parties have equivalent title and capabilities. \u000d\u000a\u2022 The shifts or partial shifts involved are equal in duration. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Both shifts included in the swap must occur within the same pay period. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Both employees acknowledge the shift swap via the department-approved process. \u000d\u000a\u2022 The request is approved by leadership before the first shift involved begins. \u000d\u000aShift Giveaways\u000d\u000aIf an employee's PTO request is denied, the employee may arrange shift coverage and \u000d\u000aprocess such as a shift giveaway if: \u000d\u000a\u2022 The accepting employee has an equivalent title and capabilities. \u000d\u000a\u2022 When giving away an overtime assignment, the receiving employee must meet the \u000d\u000ashift's minimum requirements, not the title and capabilities of the employee giving \u000d\u000athe shift away. \u000d\u000a\u2022 They have sufficient PTO available to cover the shift they intend to give away if it is a \u000d\u000aregularly scheduled shift. \u000d\u000ao If the shift giveaway applies to an overtime assignment that the requesting \u000d\u000aemployee initially accepted, the use of PTO is not required. \u000d\u000a\u2022 The request is approved by leadership before the shift begins. \u000d\u000aOnce approved, the covering employee assumes responsibility for the shift under \u000d\u000aattendance standards. ","Job Preparedness & Shift Restrictions\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 16\u000d\u000aPolicy Number: 100-05 Subject: Job Preparedness and Shift Restrictions\u000d\u000aRevision Date: November 19th, 2025 Effective Date: January 1st, 2026\u000d\u000aI. PURPOSE\u000d\u000aTo establish standards for employees to work efficiently, provide excellent service and \u000d\u000aensure high-quality performance. \u000d\u000aII. POLICY\u000d\u000aEmployees are required to arrive well-rested and capable of fulfilling the needs of the public \u000d\u000aand our patients. Maintaining alertness fosters a safe workplace and upholds high standards \u000d\u000aof service and patient care. Fatigue can negatively impact individuals and may endanger \u000d\u000aboth patients and colleagues. The use of drugs or alcohol, as well as sleeping during work \u000d\u000ahours, is strictly prohibited. Employees who are found to be in potential violation of these \u000d\u000astandards may be sent home without pay and could be subject to corrective action up to \u000d\u000aand including termination. \u000d\u000aIn some situations, an employee may be required to remain at work beyond their scheduled \u000d\u000ashift. The maximum permitted shift length is eighteen (18) hours. ","Distractions\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 17\u000d\u000aPolicy Number: 100-06 Subject: Distractions\u000d\u000aRevision Date: N/A Effective Date: January 1st, 2026\u000d\u000aI. PURPOSE\u000d\u000aTo establish standards to mitigate distractions in the workplace. \u000d\u000aII. POLICY\u000d\u000aPersonal Electronic Devices\u000d\u000aPersonal electronic devices are allowed on the communications center floor provided: \u000d\u000a\u2022 They do not inhibit the ability to perform work duties. \u000d\u000a\u2022 They remain in silent mode. \u000d\u000aThe following items/activities are strictly prohibited: \u000d\u000a\u2022 Smart glasses. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Earbuds or any listening device that isn\u2019t a company-issued headset. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Media Capture, Recording, & Streaming devices. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Making or receiving phone calls or voice messages with a personal electronic device. \u000d\u000a\u2022 The use of cell phones in any capacity by trainees or trainers while they are training.\u000d\u000aIf an employee chooses to take their break at their workstation and must utilize their cell \u000d\u000aphone to make or receive a call they are required to do so outside of the ICC. \u000d\u000aUse of Company Equipment\u000d\u000aTelevisions in the ICC are the property of GMR. Employees should not request special \u000d\u000aviewing of programming that does not involve local, state or national news events and/or \u000d\u000aweather updates. \u000d\u000aUse of Company equipment, including but not limited to computers, phones, email and \u000d\u000amessaging, for personal purposes is prohibited. There is no reasonable expectation of \u000d\u000aprivacy for the use of Company equipment. The Company may access and monitor all \u000d\u000aemployee electronic usage, such as computer applications, internet, voicemail, email and \u000d\u000amessages.","Policies 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 18\u000d\u000aThe Company will not exercise its rights as described for the purpose of investigating \u000d\u000awhether employees have engaged in activity protected by the National Labor Relations Act. \u000d\u000aStreaming \u000d\u000aEmployees are prohibited from streaming or viewing non-work-related videos or music on \u000d\u000aCompany or personal electronic devices within the ICC. \u000d\u000aSocialization \u000d\u000aCasual conversation is encouraged but must not occur across the room or distract from \u000d\u000aassigned duties. Employees should be mindful of noise levels and always avoid \u000d\u000aunprofessional conversation or language. Employees should refrain from visiting others\u2019 \u000d\u000aworkstations or departments, even during breaks. \u000d\u000aGossip and rumors has a way of spreading negativity and creating unnecessary tension. To \u000d\u000amaintain a harmonious and productive environment, it\u2019s essential to focus on clear, direct \u000d\u000acommunication and to address any concerns or questions openly. By fostering a culture of \u000d\u000arespect and transparency, we can ensure that everyone feels valued and understood, paving \u000d\u000athe way for a more collaborative and supportive workplace. ","Appearance \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 19\u000d\u000aPolicy Number: 100-07 Subject: Appearance\u000d\u000aRevision Date: January 8th, 2026 Effective Date: January 8th, 2026\u000d\u000aI. PURPOSE\u000d\u000aTo establish guidelines for dress code and overall appearance expectations for employees.\u000d\u000aII. POLICY\u000d\u000aA casual professional dress code is permitted, although leadership may require more \u000d\u000aprofessional attire when certain business needs arise. Employees are expected to maintain a \u000d\u000awell-groomed and professional appearance while at work or attending business-related \u000d\u000ameetings, courses, conferences and other events. \u000d\u000aCompany-Issued Uniform Components \u000d\u000a\u2022 Photo ID Badge \u000d\u000a\u2022 This access card will be issued to all employees and must be displayed at all times. \u000d\u000a\u2022 See policy 100-08 for additional details on this item.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Shirts \u000d\u000a\u2022 GMR polos will be issued to each employee at no cost. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Outerwear \u000d\u000a\u2022 One (1) GMR jacket will be issued to each employee at no cost. \u000d\u000aEmployee Responsibility Uniform Components \u000d\u000a\u2022 Headwear \u000d\u000ao Head scarves or other hair accessories should be solid white, tan/khaki, gray, \u000d\u000adark blue or black. \u000d\u000ao Hats must be baseball style/brimmed and bear a GMR-affiliated logo or be \u000d\u000asolid white, tan/khaki, gray, dark blue or black and free of other logos. Hats \u000d\u000amust be worn with the brim facing forward. \u000d\u000ao Sunglasses may not be worn. ","Policies 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 20\u000d\u000a\u2022 Undershirts \u000d\u000ao May be short or long sleeved \u000d\u000ao If worn, any visible part of the shirt should be solid white, tan / khaki, gray, \u000d\u000adark blue or black.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Outerwear\u000d\u000ao Employees may also choose to wear GMR branded jackets purchased from \u000d\u000athe GMR Brand Store provided that they are gray, dark blue, or black. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Pants / Skirts \u000d\u000ao Employees can wear pants/skirts of their own choosing within the guidelines \u000d\u000abelow. \u000d\u000ao Pants / Skirts should be solid white, tan/khaki, gray, dark blue or black. \u000d\u000ao While sitting, the skirt hem should remain at knee length. \u000d\u000ao Denim is allowed, but jeans must be in good condition, regardless of current \u000d\u000atrends. \u000d\u000ao No holes, faded, frayed or distressed denim. \u000d\u000ao No ill-fitting or \u201csagging\u201d jeans. \u000d\u000ao No overly embellished designs. \u000d\u000ao No shorts, athletic / leisure wear, leggings or overalls. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Footwear \u000d\u000ao Must have a non-slip sole and be clean in appearance and in good condition. \u000d\u000ao House slippers are not permitted. \u000d\u000aGeneral Appearance \u000d\u000aThe ICC is a business environment with frequent visitors. All attire must be neat, clean, free \u000d\u000aof wrinkles, and in presentable condition. \u000d\u000aOn weekdays (Monday \u2013 Friday, non-company holidays) employees must adhere to the \u000d\u000apreviously outlined dress code. \u000d\u000aOn weekends (Saturday and Sunday) and company holidays, a GMR branded t-shirt or \u000d\u000ahoodie may be worn. The other dress code expectations should still be adhered to. ","Policies 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 21\u000d\u000aPersonal Appearance and Hygiene \u000d\u000a\u2022 Hair \u000d\u000ao Must always be kept clean and neat. \u000d\u000ao Must be styled in a way that does not interfere with the field of vision or \u000d\u000aassigned duties. \u000d\u000ao Must not present an unprofessional image. Including, but not limited to: \u000d\u000a\u25aa Mohawks and other unusual styles. \u000d\u000a\u25aa Neon, glittering or multiple artificial hues visible. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Facial hair \u000d\u000ao Must be kept trimmed and tidy. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Fingernails \u000d\u000ao Must be kept neat and clean. \u000d\u000ao Length must not inhibit performance of job duties. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Jewelry \u000d\u000ao Must portray a professional image. \u000d\u000ao Must not compromise safety. \u000d\u000ao Must not inhibit performance of job duties.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Tattoos \u000d\u000ao Must be covered if they are perceived as offensive or vulgar. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Scents \u000d\u000ao All employees should take steps to avoid strong scents in the workplace. \u000d\u000aIncluding, but not limited to: \u000d\u000a\u25aa Bad breath \u000d\u000a\u25aa Body odor \u000d\u000a\u25aa Tobacco products \u000d\u000a\u25aa Heavy colognes/perfumes/lotions/essential oils \u000d\u000a\u25aa Communications staff must comply with field grooming and safety \u000d\u000apolicies if they are to attend any ride-along sessions. ","Policies 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 22\u000d\u000aReasonable Accommodations for Dress and Grooming\u000d\u000aThe Company is committed to complying with all applicable federal, state, and local laws \u000d\u000aregarding reasonable accommodations. Employees who require modifications to the dress \u000d\u000acode due to a sincerely held religious belief, observance, or practice, or because of a \u000d\u000adisability or medical condition, may request an accommodation.\u000d\u000aExamples of accommodations include, but are not limited to:\u000d\u000a\u2022 Allowing religious attire or grooming practices (e.g., hijabs, turbans, yarmulkes, \u000d\u000amodest clothing, facial hair).\u000d\u000a\u2022 Adjusting uniform requirements for medical reasons (e.g., alternative fabrics or \u000d\u000astyles to prevent irritation or accommodate medical devices).\u000d\u000aEmployees seeking an accommodation should notify their leadership and Human Resources \u000d\u000aas soon as possible. The Company will engage in an interactive process to determine a \u000d\u000areasonable solution that does not impose an undue hardship on business operations or\u000d\u000acompromise workplace safety.\u000d\u000aUniform Replacement\u000d\u000aLeadership may approve uniform replacements for wear and tear or size changes, with items \u000d\u000aexchanged on a one-to-one basis. Employees will be responsible for the cost of replacing \u000d\u000auniform items due to loss, misuse, abuse or lack of care. \u000d\u000aReturn of Uniforms\u000d\u000aAll company-issued clothing remains the property of GMR. Upon the conclusion of \u000d\u000aemployment in the ICC, employees are required to return all company-issued clothing and \u000d\u000amaterials. Failure to do so will result in the cost of these items being deducted from the final \u000d\u000apaycheck. \u000d\u000aAdditional Information\u000d\u000aIf an employee's appearance or grooming does not align with Company standards, they may \u000d\u000abe required to leave work without pay to address the issue before resuming their duties. ","Company-Issued ID Badge \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 23\u000d\u000aPolicy Number: 100-08 Subject: Company-Issued ID Badge\u000d\u000aRevision Date: November 11th, 2025 Effective Date: January 1\u000d\u000ast, 2026\u000d\u000aI. PURPOSE\u000d\u000aTo establish procedures outlining the use and possession of company-issued ID badges.\u000d\u000aII. POLICY\u000d\u000aBadge Possession and Use \u000d\u000a\u2022 Employees must always display their ID badges inside of GMR facilities. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Employees must not lend their badge to another individual for any reason. \u000d\u000a\u2022 If an employee arrives for duty without their badge, they are required to inform the \u000d\u000aon-duty leader upon arrival to request a replacement or temporary badge. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Employees are required to swipe their ID badges on any door equipped with a badge \u000d\u000areader before entry to ensure that access is properly documented; tailgating is not \u000d\u000apermitted. \u000d\u000a\u2022 All visitors, including GMR employees not based at HQ, must register at the front \u000d\u000adesk. Contact an on-duty leader for assistance. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Employees must not grant anyone access to GMR property without the approval of \u000d\u000aleadership. \u000d\u000aMissing Badge \u000d\u000aMissing ID badges present a security concern and must be reported to the on-duty leader \u000d\u000aimmediately. \u000d\u000a\u2022 The initial replacement will be provided at no cost to the employee. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Subsequent replacements may result in a $15.00 payroll deduction. \u000d\u000aReturn of Badge\u000d\u000aID badges are to be turned in to the on-duty leader upon separation of employment. ","Lockers & Personal Belongings \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 24\u000d\u000aPolicy Number: 100-09 Subject: Lockers and Personal Belongings\u000d\u000aRevision Date: November 11th, 2025 Effective Date: January 1st, 2026\u000d\u000aI. PURPOSE\u000d\u000aTo establish standards for the property of ICC employees left in lockers or in the common \u000d\u000aareas of the ICC.\u000d\u000aII. POLICY\u000d\u000aLockers\u000d\u000a\u2022 Are the property of GMR. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Will be assigned by departmental leadership. \u000d\u000a\u2022 May have to be shared by employees due to limited availability. \u000d\u000a\u2022 May only be used by the designated staff member(s). \u000d\u000a\u2022 May not have anything affixed or attached to either the interior or the exterior. \u000d\u000a\u2022 May be unlocked or reprogrammed by leadership without employee consent if \u000d\u000alocker procedures are in question or in the event of an emergency. \u000d\u000aItems prohibited from being stored in lockers include, but are not limited to:\u000d\u000a\u2022 Alcohol\u000d\u000a\u2022 Illicit Drugs\u000d\u000a\u2022 Dangerous chemicals\u000d\u000a\u2022 Flammable or explosive materials\u000d\u000a\u2022 Perishable items, such as food and beverages\u000d\u000a\u2022 Unsealed containers holding liquids of any kind\u000d\u000a\u2022 Weapons of any kind \u000d\u000aImproper use of a locker may result in the suspension or termination of locker privileges.\u000d\u000aEmployees have no reasonable expectation of privacy for items placed in lockers. Leadership \u000d\u000amay inspect items, and any contents within, at any time based on reasonable suspicion, with \u000d\u000aor without prior notice. ","Policies 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 25\u000d\u000aPersonal Belongings\u000d\u000a\u2022 Must be stored in an employee\u2019s assigned locker when off duty. \u000d\u000a\u2022 May be discarded without notice if left outside of a locker. \u000d\u000aGMR is not liable for any personal belongings, including those in lockers. The company will \u000d\u000anot reimburse employees for discarded items.\u000d\u000aEmployees are expected to cooperate in any search or inspection of their person or property \u000d\u000arequested for reasonable suspicion as described in the Company handbook. ","Condition & Upkeep of Facilities\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 26\u000d\u000aPolicy Number: 100-10 Subject: Condition and Upkeep of Facilities\u000d\u000aRevision Date: N/A Effective Date: January 1st, 2026\u000d\u000aI. PURPOSE\u000d\u000aTo establish standards and expectations of workplace cleanliness and facility upkeep.\u000d\u000aII. POLICY\u000d\u000aFood and Beverage \u000d\u000aEmployees are prohibited from storing food or beverages in locations other than in the \u000d\u000abreakroom or in personal lunch bags or coolers. The GMR HQ refrigerator policy should be \u000d\u000afollowed, including attention to the cleaning schedule. \u000d\u000aFood and beverages may be consumed at workstations if: \u000d\u000a\u2022 Work duties are not impacted. \u000d\u000a\u2022 No residue is left behind. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Equipment and furniture are not damaged. \u000d\u000aEmployees are responsible for keeping their work areas clean, including addressing spills, \u000d\u000acrumbs and overflowing trash. For cleaning supplies or assistance, employees should see an \u000d\u000aon-duty leader. \u000d\u000aMaintenance \u000d\u000aEmployees should report any malfunctioning, missing, or broken equipment, furniture, etc. \u000d\u000ato an on-duty leader. \u000d\u000aRegular Cleaning \u000d\u000aShift supervisors or their designee will inspect and clean departmental workstations \u000d\u000aregularly. Personal belongings are not permitted to be stored at any workstation, including \u000d\u000ain drawers or cabinets. Personal items left outside lockers may be discarded without notice. \u000d\u000aGMR is not liable for any personal belongings, including those in lockers. The Company will \u000d\u000anot reimburse employees for damaged, discarded, lost or missing items. ","Tobacco & Smoke-Free Workplace\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 27\u000d\u000aPolicy Number: 100-11 Subject: Tobacco and Smoke-Free Workplace\u000d\u000aRevision Date: November 19th, 2025 Effective Date: January 1st, 2026\u000d\u000aI. PURPOSE\u000d\u000aTo establish a policy regarding tobacco or synthetic product use when reporting for and \u000d\u000awhile on duty in the ICC. \u000d\u000aII. POLICY\u000d\u000aTo ensure a safe, healthy workplace, all tobacco products, including, but not limited to those \u000d\u000aas defined below, are prohibited in company workspaces, common areas and company \u000d\u000avehicles. This policy applies to all employees, clients, contractors and visitors. \u000d\u000a\u2022 The term \u201csmoking\u201d refers to the burning of all forms of tobacco included in \u000d\u000acigarettes, cigars, and pipes.\u000d\u000a\u2022 The term \u201csmokeless tobacco\u201d refers to non-burning forms of tobacco and \u000d\u000asynthetics, including chewing tobacco and electronic cigarettes/vapes. \u000d\u000aUsers should do their best to be free of the scent of tobacco or synthetics on their person \u000d\u000awhen reporting for duty and at the conclusion of each break should they partake during \u000d\u000atheir break. \u000d\u000aSmoking and the use of smokeless tobacco products is solely permitted in designated \u000d\u000aoutdoor areas during scheduled break times. \u000d\u000aAll tobacco products and associated paraphernalia must be stored out of sight while in \u000d\u000aCompany facilities or vehicles. \u000d\u000aBreak schedules will not be modified to accommodate smoking or tobacco use. ","Phoenix: Tobacco & Electronic Cigarettes\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 28\u000d\u000aPolicy Number: N/A Subject: Phoenix: Tobacco and Electronic Cigarettes\u000d\u000aRevision Date: N/A Effective Date: N/A\u000d\u000aI. PURPOSE\u000d\u000aThe Communication Center policy is to provide a safe and pleasant environment for our \u000d\u000acustomers and employees. With this in mind, the use of tobacco and electronic smoking \u000d\u000aproducts are restricted unless otherwise governed by applicable law.\u000d\u000aII. POLICY\u000d\u000a1. Any type of smoking and the use of smokeless tobacco is only allowed in designated \u000d\u000asmoking areas during designated break times.\u000d\u000a2. Designated smoking area for the Communications Center is the West side of the \u000d\u000abuilding at the curb and beyond.\u000d\u000a3. No designated area is allowed inside of the Communications Center\u000d\u000a4. Within the designated smoking area smokers are to use the disposal method \u000d\u000aprovided for cigarettes. The area is to be kept clean of trash and any smoking \u000d\u000amaterial.\u000d\u000a5. The sale of tobacco and electronic smoking products on company premises by \u000d\u000avending or other means is also prohibited.\u000d\u000a6. No smoking within 100 feet of the building. \u000d\u000aAny employee who violates this policy may be subject to corrective action, up to and \u000d\u000aincluding termination.\u000d\u000aIII.TOBACCO USE IMPLICATIONS\u000d\u000a1. The use of tobacco products will impact the rates you pay for the company provided \u000d\u000amedical plans. \u000d\u000a2. For those interested in quitting, referral programs are available. Please contact the \u000d\u000abenefits Service Center at 1-888-301-2123 for details, Designated smoking area for \u000d\u000athe Communications Center is the West side of the building at the curb and beyond. ","Inclement Weather\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 29\u000d\u000aPolicy Number: 100-12 Subject: Inclement Weather\u000d\u000aRevision Date: November 19th, 2025 Effective Date: January 1st, 2026\u000d\u000aI. PURPOSE\u000d\u000aTo establish a procedure to maintain adequate staffing at all times, regardless of weather, \u000d\u000aand to outline expectations when lodging accommodations are made for inclement \u000d\u000aconditions. \u000d\u000aII. POLICY\u000d\u000aGMR requires all essential personnel to report for their scheduled shift regardless of \u000d\u000aweather conditions.\u000d\u000aIII.PROCEDURE\u000d\u000aGMR\u2019s mission statement is to provide care to the world at a moment\u2019s notice. Although \u000d\u000asevere weather or disasters may make commuting to work challenging, employees are \u000d\u000arequired to report for duty unless instructed otherwise. \u000d\u000aDuring periods of inclement weather, employees are advised to allocate sufficient time to \u000d\u000aarrive at work for the start of their scheduled shift. Employees on duty may be expected to \u000d\u000aremain until their replacement has arrived. \u000d\u000aEmployees are responsible for planning for inclement weather. Tardiness or absences will \u000d\u000anot be excused due to weather events and failure to report for duty when accommodations \u000d\u000ahave been offered will count as an Occurrence of Significant Impact per the Attendance \u000d\u000aPolicy. \u000d\u000aThe Company will provide reasonable lodging accommodation when deemed necessary. \u000d\u000aEmployees must agree to all stipulated terms prior to accepting the offer of companysponsored accommodation. Those stipulations are: \u000d\u000a\u2022 Employees must act professionally as company representatives during GMRsponsored stays. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Booking confirmations are sent to the employee\u2019s GMR email address. \u000d\u000a\u2022 A government-issued ID is required for check-in. ","Policies 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 30\u000d\u000a\u2022 GMR covers accommodation and taxes. Employees must present a credit or debit \u000d\u000acard at check-in for an incidental hold. Hold amounts and refund timing vary by hotel \u000d\u000apolicy. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Employees are responsible for any expenses beyond the room rate and taxes, \u000d\u000aincluding but not limited to: \u000d\u000ao Additional fees charged if an employee elects to bring their pet(s). \u000d\u000ao Charges for missing items or damaged contents of the room. \u000d\u000ao Room service or incidental fees charged to the room.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Due to limited hotel availability, it may not be possible to place all staff in the same \u000d\u000ahotel.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Transportation between the hotel and office will be the responsibility of each \u000d\u000aemployee. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Employees are expected to arrive equipped with all necessary items required to stay \u000d\u000athroughout the entirety of the weather event. These provisions may include, but are \u000d\u000anot limited to: \u000d\u000ao Food \u000d\u000ao Beverages \u000d\u000ao Toiletries \u000d\u000ao Extra work clothes \u000d\u000ao Outerwear, including appropriate footwear for the expected weather\u000d\u000a\u2022 Snacks, sandwich-making material, and various microwaveable food options may be \u000d\u000aavailable while on duty. \u000d\u000ao Off-duty meals are not provided. \u000d\u000ao Employees should bring their own food to accommodate any personal dietary \u000d\u000aneeds or preferences. ","Lactation Accommodation\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 31\u000d\u000aPolicy Number: 100-13 Subject: Lactation Accommodation \u000d\u000aRevision Date: N/A Effective Date: January 1st, 2026\u000d\u000aI. PURPOSE\u000d\u000aTo establish departmental expectations and procedures for lactation accommodations in \u000d\u000aalignment with the GMR Employee Handbook. \u000d\u000aII. POLICY\u000d\u000aThis policy ensures compliance with applicable laws and supports employees returning to \u000d\u000awork after childbirth who require lactation accommodations. \u000d\u000aEmployees needing lactation accommodations should notify their Leader upon returning to \u000d\u000awork following childbirth. Upon notification, departmental leadership will meet with the \u000d\u000aemployee to review the request and coordinate appropriate arrangements that balance \u000d\u000aoperational needs and legal requirements.\u000d\u000aIII.PROCEDURE\u000d\u000aBreak Time\u000d\u000aEmployees may take reasonable break time to express milk. When possible, these breaks \u000d\u000ashould coincide with existing break periods. Additional unpaid break time may be arranged \u000d\u000aand must be accurately recorded using the Company\u2019s timekeeping system. \u000d\u000aPrivate Lactation Space\u000d\u000aThe Company will provide access to a private, non-bathroom space that is shielded from \u000d\u000aview and free from intrusion. This space will be equipped for milk expression, including \u000d\u000aseating, electrical outlets, and surfaces as needed. \u000d\u000aMilk Storage \u000d\u000aEmployees may use personal cooler packs or store expressed milk in a designated \u000d\u000arefrigerator/freezer. All containers must be clearly labeled with the employee\u2019s name and \u000d\u000adate. Employees are responsible for removing containers at the end of each shift. GMR is \u000d\u000anot liable for items left in shared spaces. ","Policies 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 32\u000d\u000aLegal Compliance \u000d\u000aIn jurisdictions with specific lactation accommodation laws, the Company will comply with \u000d\u000aall applicable requirements, including providing greater or different benefits than those \u000d\u000aoutlined here. ","Respect in the Workplace\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 33\u000d\u000aThe importance of Respect in the Workplace\u000d\u000a\u2022 Provides a feeling of security at work\u000d\u000a\u2022 Shows appreciation for patients, coworkers, and leaders\u000d\u000a\u2022 Maintains efficiency\u000d\u000a\u2022 Fosters a happy work environment\u000d\u000aHow to Foster Respect\u000d\u000aAvoid gossip\u000d\u000aBe mindful of \u000d\u000aeveryone\u2019s feelings\u000d\u000aShow appreciation \u000d\u000ato each other\u000d\u000aGreet everyone \u000d\u000awith kindness\u000d\u000aValue diversity and\u000d\u000aother\u2019s opinions\u000d\u000aThe Main Floor\u000d\u000aRules\u000d\u000a1. Use teams when collaborating with coworkers, whenever possible\u000d\u000a2. When you do need to talk on the floor, please speak as quiet as possible\u000d\u000a3. No horseplay or other noisy activities will be tolerated\u000d\u000aWhy?\u000d\u000a\u2022 Helps maintain a professional work environment\u000d\u000a\u2022 Assists dispatchers and nurse navigating with hearing patient needs, while on the phone\u000d\u000a\u2022 Assists with keeping patient\u2019s calm when there is minimal background noise\u000d\u000aTeams Decorum\u000d\u000a1. 911 Nurse Navigation promotes a collaborative work environment when tryingto aid our \u000d\u000apatients or troubleshoot issues we may have run into.\u000d\u000a2. This will be a no judgment zone!\u000d\u000a3. Feel free to see if others may have handled the situation differently or letus know how \u000d\u000ayou are feeling about a particular situation.\u000d\u000a4. This forum is also useful to discuss obstacles you may have experienced.\u000d\u000a5. Let\u2019s troubleshoot and work together.\u000d\u000aCambridge dictionary \u000d\u000adefines respect as:\u000d\u000a\u201cto treat something or \u000d\u000asomeone with kindness \u000d\u000aand care\u201d.","Contracts, Territories, & Licensing\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 34\u000d\u000aPlease see the Contract Quick Links section for a full list of the territories we serve. \u000d\u000a911 Contracts\u000d\u000a\u2022 Fire Departments handle Emergency Medical Services\u000d\u000a\u2022 NN is typically contracted through County Fire and Rescue\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Sometimes as stand-alone solution\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Sometimes in conjunction with AMR ground transport services\u000d\u000ao AMR offers 911 call center, emergency dispatch, and emergent/nonemergent transport solutions\u000d\u000aLicensure\u000d\u000aCompact Licenses Non-Compact License\u000d\u000aCompact licensure covers most of our bigger \u000d\u000acontracts\u000d\u000aStates not covered\u000d\u000a\u2022 CA, DC, NY, OR, MI\u000d\u000aPlease provide the following by the end of your first week of employment with GMR:\u000d\u000a\u2022 Marriage and/or divorce certificates\u000d\u000a\u2022 How to order official school transcripts (high school diploma needed for LVNs)\u000d\u000a\u2022 Name and/or gender change documents\u000d\u000a\u2022 List of schools attended\u000d\u000a\u2022 We will do fingerprint hard cards in house (must bring a photo ID)","Page 35\u000d\u000aAbout GMR\u000d\u000aIn This Section\u000d\u000aDiscover the purpose and drive that makes GMR an incredible place to work. Each call we \u000d\u000amanage, and each concern we resolve, helps our neighbors engage with an improved \u000d\u000asystem of health care; one where they are valued, heard, invited to engage with the \u000d\u000aresources of their communities. Thank you for being a member of our team! ","Reference Topics\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 36\u000d\u000aWelcome 911 Nurse Navigation\u000d\u000aIntroduction\u000d\u000aOur Vision & Mission\u000d\u000aCore Behaviors\u000d\u000aMeet Our Team\u000d\u000aCompany Jargon\u000d\u000a911 Nurse Navigation (NN) Deep Dive","Welcome to 911 Nurse Navigation\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 37\u000d\u000aDear Team Member\u000d\u000aWelcome to 911 Nurse Navigation at Global Medical Response (GMR)!\u000d\u000aI am excited to welcome you to our team and thank you for choosing to join us. As a Nurse \u000d\u000aNavigator, you play a critical role in helping patients access the right level of care at the right \u000d\u000atime. Every interaction you have has the potential to provide reassurance, guidance, and \u000d\u000asupport to individuals and families during moments when they need it most.\u000d\u000aAt 911 Nurse Navigation, our mission is centered on delivering exceptional clinical guidance \u000d\u000awhile promoting patient safety, improving healthcare access, and supporting appropriate care \u000d\u000adecisions. We are proud of the work we do and the positive impact we make every day across \u000d\u000athe communities we serve.\u000d\u000aAs you begin your journey with us, I encourage you to embrace the opportunities to learn, ask \u000d\u000aquestions, and collaborate with your colleagues. We believe that success comes from \u000d\u000acontinuous learning, teamwork, accountability, and a shared commitment to excellence. Your \u000d\u000aunique experiences, skills, and perspectives are valued and will contribute to the ongoing \u000d\u000asuccess of our program.\u000d\u000aOur leadership team is committed to creating an environment where team members feel \u000d\u000asupported, respected, and empowered to grow professionally. Throughout your onboarding and \u000d\u000abeyond, you will have access to leaders, educators, and peers who are invested in your success.\u000d\u000aWe recognize that starting a new role can be both exciting and challenging. Please know that \u000d\u000ayou are not expected to know everything on day one. Give yourself grace as you learn new \u000d\u000asystems, processes, and workflows. We are here to support you every step of the way.\u000d\u000aThank you for bringing your clinical expertise, compassion, and dedication to our organization. \u000d\u000aWe are honored to have you as part of the 911 Nurse Navigation family and look forward to the \u000d\u000acontributions you will make.\u000d\u000aWelcome aboard. We are excited to have you with us.\u000d\u000aWarm regards,\u000d\u000aPurity Nyaga\u000d\u000aDirector, Clinical Operations\u000d\u000a911 Nurse Navigation","Introduction\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 38\u000d\u000a \u000d\u000aGlobal Medical Response delivers comprehensive emergency medical services to over five \u000d\u000amillion patients annually. Our extensive network of ground and air clinical teams ensures the \u000d\u000aright level of care at the right time and place, regardless of the situation. With a focus on patient \u000d\u000acare and emergency response, GMR stands out as a leader in the emergency medical services \u000d\u000aindustry.\u000d\u000aMost Experienced Program Offering More Complete Care to 911 Callers\u000d\u000aAn estimated 30% of calls to 911 don\u2019t need an immediate EMS response. These callers need \u000d\u000ahelp, but often don\u2019t know where else to go, or they aren\u2019t able to access the care they need.\u000d\u000aIn the past, the only method communities had to help callers with non-life-threatening needs \u000d\u000awas to dispatch EMS and send the patient to the Emergency Department (ED). This diverted \u000d\u000aEMS resources from urgent, life-threatening issues and led to higher costs for patients who \u000d\u000adidn\u2019t require a visit to the ED.\u000d\u000aIn 2018, Global Medical Response (GMR) pioneered a solution with its introduction of 911 \u000d\u000aNurse Navigation in order to provide care to these callers, often without the use of an \u000d\u000aambulance. In communities across the country, GMR\u2019s Nurse Navigators use evidence-based \u000d\u000aclinical protocols to screen a patient\u2019s current condition and provide an appropriate resource to \u000d\u000ameet the caller\u2019s unique healthcare needs. \u000d\u000aResolutions include; dispatching a ride-share to an urgent care accepting patients, an \u000d\u000aappointment at a Federally Qualified Health Center, or virtual care with a physician on the spot.\u000d\u000aLearn more on our website at: \u000d\u000a\ud83d\udd17 https://globalmedicalresponse.com/services/healthcare-innovation/nurse-navigatio","About GMR 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 39\u000d\u000aBetter for Patients and Communities\u000d\u000aIn 2024, more than 50,000 911 callers from across the country were screened by GMR\u2019s 911 \u000d\u000aNurse Navigation program and redirected to more clinically appropriate and cost-effective care \u000d\u000aoptions.\u000d\u000aEvery 10 minutes someone called 911 seeking help and GMR\u2019s\u000d\u000ateam of 911 Nurse Navigators connected them to the best \u000d\u000ahealthcare resource\u000d\u000a$21 million estimated in savings for patients, first response \u000d\u000aagencies, payors and health systems\u000d\u000a81,000-unit hours of capacity back into the EMS system by avoiding \u000d\u000aunnecessary responses, ambulance transports and ED visits","About GMR 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 40\u000d\u000aBetter for EMS Providers\u000d\u000aOur first responders in 911 Nurse Navigation markets are also more satisfied with their work. \u000d\u000aGMR\u2019s data indicates decreased burnout and improved satisfaction when providers are not \u000d\u000aoverly burdened with low acuity calls. \u000d\u000aIn GMR\u2019s 911 Nurse Navigation markets:\u000d\u000a4.5% increase in field \u000d\u000aproviders who stated they \u000d\u000afeel like their job is important\u000d\u000a6.0% increase in field \u000d\u000aproviders who stated they \u000d\u000afeel like their training and \u000d\u000askills are well utilized\u000d\u000a11.6% increase in field \u000d\u000aproviders who stated they \u000d\u000ahave high job satisfaction\u000d\u000a4.5% 6.0%\u000d\u000a11.6%","Our Vision & Mission\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 41\u000d\u000aOur Vision\u000d\u000aWe will provide a healthier tomorrow for millions of people, one patient at a time, by providing \u000d\u000aaccess to the right care and serving as a trusted EMS healthcare partner in every community.\u000d\u000aOur Mission\u000d\u000aProviding care to the world at a moment\u2019s notice","Core Behaviors\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 42\u000d\u000aGMR Core Behaviors Outline\u000d\u000aKEEP CARE \u000d\u000aAT THE CENTER\u000d\u000aRAISE YOUR \u000d\u000aHAND\u000d\u000aSEEK TO \u000d\u000aUNDERSTAND\u000d\u000aFIND A WAY \u000d\u000aTOGETHER\u000d\u000aBE \u000d\u000aACCOUNTABLE\u000d\u000aWe prioritize the care \u000d\u000aof our patients and \u000d\u000aour teams when we \u000d\u000aplan or act.\u000d\u000aWe ensure that people \u000d\u000acan feely and safely \u000d\u000a\u201craise their hands\u201d \u000d\u000aabout issues, \u000d\u000aconcerns, and \u000d\u000aopportunities \u2013 and it \u000d\u000ais everyone\u2019s duty to \u000d\u000ado so. \u000d\u000aWe treat each other \u000d\u000arespectfully. We gather \u000d\u000ainformation, listen and \u000d\u000aseek to understand \u000d\u000abefore acting\u000d\u000aWe work together to \u000d\u000asolve problems and \u000d\u000afind solutions that \u000d\u000asupport our mission.\u000d\u000aWe set clear \u000d\u000aexpectations, systems, \u000d\u000aand processes and \u000d\u000atrust those closest to \u000d\u000athe issue to make \u000d\u000agood decisions and \u000d\u000atake accountability. \u000d\u000aFor more information, visit the GMR Home Page on Sharepoint.","Meet Our Team\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 43\u000d\u000aOrganizational Chart\u000d\u000aFull Organizational Chart: \ud83d\udd17911 Nurse Navigation Organizational Chart\u000d\u000aOur Leadership Team\u000d\u000aPatient-Facing Teams","About GMR 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 44\u000d\u000aOperations\u000d\u000aCustomer Success","Company Jargon\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 45\u000d\u000aACW\u000d\u000aAfter Call Work\u000d\u000aThis is the designated time after disconnecting with the caller / dispatcher to \u000d\u000acomplete documentation related to the call. \u000d\u000a\u2022 A five-minute timer will start immediately after the call has ended. When \u000d\u000athe timer ends, the nurse will be automatically placed back On-Queue to \u000d\u000areceive another call. \u000d\u000a\u2022 If the nurse completes documentation before the timer ends, the nurse \u000d\u000awill click the blue done button to go back on-queue.\u000d\u000aAdditional details about ACW can be reviewed in our Genesys software tutorial.\u000d\u000aALS\u000d\u000aAdvanced Life Support\u000d\u000aThis response is for immediate life threats. Onboard an ambulance with lights \u000d\u000aand sirens are paramedics and EMTS who are trained to intervene and have \u000d\u000aaccess to life-saving meds and equipment. The main reasons we call are for loss \u000d\u000aof consciousness, hemorrhage, stroke, chest pain (MI), and respiratory distress.\u000d\u000aAMR\u000d\u000aAmerican Medical Response\u000d\u000aOur ground transportation company which responds to emergencies and \u000d\u000aconducts interfacility transfers.","About GMR 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 46\u000d\u000aBLS\u000d\u000aBasic Life Support\u000d\u000aThis response type means an ambulance has been dispatched with limited \u000d\u000aability for intervention (no IVs, no meds, no intubation). Crew typically consists \u000d\u000aof two EMTs who provide basic CPR and first aid.\u000d\u000aCAD\u000d\u000aComputer Aided Dispatch\u000d\u000aDispatchers use this to send calls over to 911 Nurse Navigation (NN) and to Fire\u000d\u000a/ EMS via computer. We have 5 contracts that are CAD-to-CAD:\u000d\u000a\u2022 DCFEMS \u000d\u000a\u2022 Rochester\u000d\u000a\u2022 Onondaga\u000d\u000a\u2022 Dekalb\u000d\u000a\u2022 Heartland \u000d\u000aWhen calls come through the CAD, click it on the right side of the screen to grab \u000d\u000ait and click being evaluated to claim it as yours.\u000d\u000aFor more information, please review our CAD-to-CAD software tutorial. \u000d\u000aCRISP\u000d\u000aChesapeake Regional Information System\u000d\u000aCRISP is a regional health information exchange (HIE) serving Maryland and the \u000d\u000aDistrict of Columbia. We use CRISP to find (DC only) patient\u2019s insurance ID \u000d\u000anumbers and home clinics. You must log in once monthly to maintain access.\u000d\u000aPlease review our CRISP DC software tutorial for more information. ","About GMR 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 47\u000d\u000aCSM\u000d\u000aCustomer Success Manager\u000d\u000aThis team is client (contract) facing. They ensure clear communication and \u000d\u000acollaboration between the client and 911 NN. There are four who are assigned \u000d\u000ato certain regions of the United States and conduct quarter meetings called \u000d\u000aJOCs with each contract. This team is managed by Namon Huddleston, AVP \u000d\u000aClient Success.\u000d\u000aDC FEMS\u000d\u000aDistrict of Columbia Fire and Emergency Services\u000d\u000aOur first NN contract in 2018. Located in the US Capital. \u000d\u000a\u2022 They have a distinct phone greeting:\u000d\u000a\u27a2 \u201cRight Care, right now this is nurse [name]. How can I help you?\u201d\u000d\u000aEACW\u000d\u000aExtended After Call Work\u000d\u000aThis Genesys status allows nurses to complete call-related tasks such as \u000d\u000aTransport.net, DC Taxi, etc. \u000d\u000a\u2022 This is a manual status change and should only be selected if the \u000d\u000astandard ACW timer is running out. Nurses should not immediately enter \u000d\u000athis status when the call is disconnected.","About GMR 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 48\u000d\u000aEMD\u000d\u000aEmergency Medical Dispatch\u000d\u000aRefers to a set of protocols used by emergency dispatchers to handle medical \u000d\u000aemergencies. It involves asking specific questions to assess the patient\u2019s \u000d\u000acondition, prioritizing the call based on severity and determining if the call \u000d\u000ameets criteria for 911 Nurse Navigation.\u000d\u000aEMS\u000d\u000aEmergency Medical Services\u000d\u000aThis is an ambulance response. EMS is further broken down into ALS and BLS \u000d\u000aresponse types.\u000d\u000aFQHC\u000d\u000aFederally Qualified Health Center\u000d\u000aThey provide comprehensive healthcare services to underserved communities \u000d\u000aregardless of ability to pay. They receive federal funding and offer a sliding fee \u000d\u000apay scale based on income and family size.\u000d\u000aGMR\u000d\u000aGlobal Medical Response\u000d\u000aThe company you work for! \u000d\u000aAs a provider of care to the world at a moment\u2019s notice, we are a leader in the \u000d\u000aemergency medical services industry.","About GMR 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 49\u000d\u000aICC\u000d\u000aIntegrated Communications Center\u000d\u000aThe call center (at headquarters in Lewisville) containing air and ground \u000d\u000acommunications and 911 Nurse Navigation.\u000d\u000aNMTARA\u000d\u000aNeeds Matched Time Appropriate Resource Allocation\u000d\u000aThis is how we determine the time to care. An NMTARA level (level 0-6) is \u000d\u000areached by selecting the appropriate Corti pathway that corresponds with the \u000d\u000apatient\u2019s most urgent complaint.\u000d\u000a\u2022 NMTARA 0: Emergent care needed (immediately) \u000d\u000a\u2022 NMTARA 1: Care needed within 1 hour \u000d\u000a\u2022 NMTARA 2: Care needed within 2-4 hours \u000d\u000a\u2022 NMTARA 3: Care needed within 12 hours \u000d\u000a\u2022 NMTARA 4: Care needed within 24 hours \u000d\u000a\u2022 NMTARA 5: Care needed within 1 week\u000d\u000aNN\u000d\u000a911 Nurse Navigation\u000d\u000aAlso called Nurse Nav. This is us!\u000d\u000aNNRide-ER\u000d\u000a911 Nurse Navigation Ride ER\u000d\u000aThis disposition is the rideshare to the emergency room. We primarily use Lyft \u000d\u000abut also use Uber. This disposition is not an option in DC (use DC Taxi or Medical \u000d\u000aTransportation Management (MTM))","About GMR 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 50\u000d\u000aNTL\u000d\u000aNurse Triage Line\u000d\u000aThis is the terminology used for 911 Nurse Navigation in the DC market. \u000d\u000a\u2022 We use this distinct phone greeting for these communications:\u000d\u000a\u27a2 \u201cRight Care, right now this is nurse [name]. How can I help you?\u201d\u000d\u000aNURSYS\u000d\u000aNursys is the only national database for verification of nurse licensure, discipline \u000d\u000aand practice privileges for RNs and LPN / VNs licensed in participating boards of \u000d\u000anursing, including all states in the Nurse Licensure Compact (NLC). \u000d\u000a\ud83d\udd17Nursys.com provides online verification for endorsement to a nurse \u000d\u000arequesting to practice in another state and anyone who wants to verify a nurse \u000d\u000alicense.\u000d\u000aOUC\u000d\u000aOffice of Unified Communications\u000d\u000aThis is the PSAP in DC.\u000d\u000aPSAP\u000d\u000aPublic Safety Answering Point\u000d\u000aThis is the 911 call center. 911 calls are dispatched from here directly to Fire /\u000d\u000aEMS or 911 Nurse Navigation. Each contract has at least one PSAP. They handle \u000d\u000aover 200 million 911 calls annually.","About GMR 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 51\u000d\u000aREF\u000d\u000aReferral\u000d\u000aThis disposition refers patients to a brick-and-mortar clinic like an urgent care or \u000d\u000abehavioral health resource like Crisis Connection.\u000d\u000aRONA\u000d\u000aRing Offered No Answer\u000d\u000aThis is a missed call. The nurse was available in Genesys but did not answer the \u000d\u000aphone. The nurse will need to place themselves back On-Queue to exit the Not\u000d\u000aResponding status.\u000d\u000aRSC\u000d\u000aReturn to Self-Care\u000d\u000aThis disposition is selected when patients opt to follow the home-care \u000d\u000ainstructions provided by the nurse or when patients decline all options \u000d\u000aincluding an EMS response. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Patients may also opt to go to the ER by private vehicle as well which \u000d\u000awould be an RSC\u000d\u000aSBARF\u000d\u000aSituation, Background, Assessment, Recommendation, Follow Through\u000d\u000aThis is standardized documentation used by nursing that borrows from the \u000d\u000atraditional SBAR format.\u000d\u000aFor more information, please review our SBARF documentation segment.","About GMR 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 52\u000d\u000aTL;DR\u000d\u000aToo Long; Didn\u2019t Read\u000d\u000aUsed to present a summary for those who possess an innate or learned \u000d\u000aaversion to reading. \u000d\u000aTNC \u000d\u000aTriage Not Complete \u000d\u000aNo NMTARA level is reached due to the following reasons: \u000d\u000a\u2022 Caller hangs up and no answer on callback x2\u000d\u000a\u2022 Patient refuses triage process\u000d\u000a\u2022 EMS arrives on scene\u000d\u000a\u2022 Exclusion list criteria met. \u000d\u000aThis replaces the former internal designation NMTARA 6.\u000d\u000aUKG \u000d\u000aUltimate Kronos Group \u000d\u000aThis chiclet is how you clock in and out, fix missed punches, check the schedule, \u000d\u000aand enter PTO requests. You can also clock in and out using the time clock on \u000d\u000athe wall near the printer.\u000d\u000aVC \u000d\u000aVirtual Care\u000d\u000aThis tele-health option is great for patients who need further evaluation \u000d\u000awithout labs / imaging. RelyMD (the company we use) works like Uber for \u000d\u000aproviders. This disposition allows patients to be treated in place. They can even \u000d\u000aget (certain) prescriptions called in to their pharmacy.","911 Nurse Navigation (NN) Deep Dive\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 53\u000d\u000a911 Traditional Model: You Call, We Haul!\u000d\u000aTimeframe: Emergency\u000d\u000aResource: Ambulance\u000d\u000a911 Call EMD EMS Response ED Transport\u000d\u000a\u2022 Caller in need contacts 911\u000d\u000a\u2022 The answering 911 Emergency Call Dispatcher asks \u000d\u000aEmergency Medical Dispatch questions\u000d\u000a\u2022 Fire department sends paramedic / EMTs to the scene\u000d\u000a\u2022 Pt treated in place or transported to the hospital for \u000d\u000afurther eval \u000d\u000a\u27a2 The individual in need may decline care\u000d\u000a\u2022 All medical 911 calls treated as emergency w/ \u000d\u000aambulance sent to patient\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Not all ambulances responses are the same!\u000d\u000ao ALS\u000d\u000ao BLS\u000d\u000aCurrent Challenges the Traditional Model Faces\u000d\u000a\u2022 Shrinking workforce: COVID prompted drastic exodus from EMS positions\u000d\u000a\u2022 Skyrocketing expenses: wages, vehicle maintenance, gas, technology\u000d\u000a\u2022 Stagnant revenues: Reimbursements have not kept pace with rising costs\u000d\u000a\u2022 Ever increasing demand from:\u000d\u000a\u2022 Growing public\u000d\u000a\u2022 Uninsured and under-insured patients\u000d\u000a\u2022 Growing medical illiteracy \u000d\u000aThis traditional model \u000d\u000acannot keep up with \u000d\u000amodern changes, concerns, \u000d\u000aor capacity needs.\u000d\u000aConsider the modern \u000d\u000achallenges of maintaining \u000d\u000athis model. Think about \u000d\u000achallenges you have faced \u000d\u000ain your career caused by \u000d\u000aresource limitations. ","About GMR 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 54\u000d\u000aOur Modern Model \u000d\u000aTimeframe: Emergency\u000d\u000aResource: Ambulance\u000d\u000a911 Call EMD EMS Response ED Transport\u000d\u000aLow Accuity Call Needs Time Options Resource Options\u000d\u000aNurse Interview\u000d\u000aNurse Navigator\u000d\u000aMatch Emergency Referral to ALS or BLS\u000d\u000aProprietary\u000d\u000aclosed-ended\u000d\u000aprotocols to ensure \u000d\u000aconsistency and \u000d\u000apatient safety.\u000d\u000aWe navigate, \u000d\u000awe don\u2019t triage\u000d\u000aThe < 1 Hour Referral to telehealth\u000d\u000aAppropriate 2 \u2013 4 Hours Referral to Urgent Care\u000d\u000aResource 12+ Hours Referral to Primary Care\u000d\u000aAllocation 24+ Hours Self-care Instructions\u000d\u000a(0 - 5)\u000d\u000a\u2022 911 NN started as a little project within \u201cIntegrated Health\u201d, a GMR department linked to \u000d\u000aseveral patient care projects\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Example: Medically at Home, Envision Physician Services, etc.\u000d\u000a\u2022 COVID-19 saw NN pursue all kinds of services:\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Medical screenings\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Worker\u2019s Comp claims\u000d\u000a\u27a2 After-hours triage for MD offices\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Other similar services\u000d\u000a\u2022 Most of these ancillary services ended by 2023 coupled by rapid growth in the 911 space\u000d\u000a\u2022 In 2025, GMR executive leadership refocused GMR from transport to healthcare and \u000d\u000apositioned 911 NN as the \u201cscaffolding on which EMS 2.0 can be built.\u201d","About GMR 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 55\u000d\u000aThe Ideal 911 Nurse Navigator\u000d\u000aShows Empathy Advocates\u000d\u000aActively Listens Educates\u000d\u000a\u201cI\u2019m so sorry you\u2019re going \u000d\u000athrough this\u2026\u201d\u000d\u000a\u201cThe van must be \u000d\u000awheelchair accessible \u2026\u201d\u000d\u000a\u201cCan you tell me more \u000d\u000aabout\u2026.?\u201d\u000d\u000a\u201cI am recommending a \u000d\u000avirtual visit because\u2026\u201d","About GMR 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 56\u000d\u000aInvestigates Follows Through\u000d\u000aWe match the patient\u2019s need to care \u000d\u000aresources. It\u2019s not just a GMR core value, it \u000d\u000ais core to the nursing profession!\u000d\u000a\u201c Yes, this clinic does offer \u000d\u000adental services\u201d\u000d\u000a\u201cYour ride is on the way and \u000d\u000athe driver\u2019s name is\u2026\u201d","About GMR 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 57\u000d\u000aLow Acuity Callers\u000d\u000aWe give low acuity callers treatment options without engaging EMS\u000d\u000aMost low acuity callers:\u000d\u000aWe know:\u000d\u000a\u2022 7-8% of 911 EMS calls need time-sensitive, life-saving intervention.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Conservative estimates show 30-40% of low-acuity, non-emergent calls can be resolved \u000d\u000aoutside an ED: Urgent Care, Virtual Care, BMH services, social services.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Less conservative estimates have this at 70-90%.\u000d\u000aWhen we fulfill our purpose, secondary benefits include:\u000d\u000a\u2022 More ambulances available for emergency calls\u000d\u000a\u2022 Less ER crowding\u000d\u000a\u2022 Increased patient satisfaction\u000d\u000a\u2022 Increased EMS provider satisfaction\u000d\u000a911 Nurse Navigation Growth\u000d\u000a\u2022 5 contracts in implementation\u000d\u000a\u2022 10 in negotiation\u000d\u000a\u2022 10+ being pursued\u000d\u000a\u2022 Current contracts looking to increase \u000d\u000avolume:\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Expand determinants\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Start field services\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Implement CAD-CAD","Contracts Quick Links\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 58\u000d\u000a \u000d\u000aWe are working hard to deliver the Contracts Quick Links Update. Thank \u000d\u000ayou for your patients. The wait will be worth it! ","Page 59\u000d\u000aWorkflows\u000d\u000aIn This Section\u000d\u000aThis section explains different call types and how we process them. \u000d\u000aThe call flow process is outlined in the Conversation Guide and \u000d\u000aincludes required talking points and reminders for each step of the \u000d\u000acall. This section also includes resources for documentation, call \u000d\u000ahandling, and the QA rubric.","Reference Topics\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 60\u000d\u000aCall Types\u000d\u000aIdentifying the Patient\u2019s Complaint\u000d\u000aExclusion List\u000d\u000aLeading with Empathy\u000d\u000aDe-Escalation\u000d\u000aConversation Guide\u000d\u000aPotential Call Barriers\u000d\u000aFrequently Asked Questions (FAQ)\u000d\u000aDispositions\u000d\u000aDocumentation Do\u2019s and Don\u2019ts\u000d\u000aFollow-Up\u000d\u000aQuality Assurance \u000d\u000aTransportation Guide","Call Types\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 61\u000d\u000a911 Call FLD (Field Fire) AMR (Field AMR)\u000d\u000a911 Call Reported \u000d\u000afrom EMD Center\u000d\u000aReferral from on-scene Fire \u000d\u000aDepartment or EMS staff\u000d\u000aReferral from on-scene \u000d\u000aAMR Staff","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 62\u000d\u000a911 Call\u000d\u000aThe quality of your interview with the patient will determine: \u000d\u000a\u2022 If the caller needs an ambulance\u000d\u000a\u27a2 If EMD needs to use lights / sirens if an ambulance is required\u000d\u000a\u2022 Is the patient\u2019s condition life threatening\u000d\u000a\u27a2 What care resources match the patient\u2019s complaint. ","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 63\u000d\u000aFLD (Field Fire)\u000d\u000a\u2022 ALS / BLS response requested by 911 dispatch\u000d\u000a\u2022 Paramedic / EMT on scene evaluated pt to be alternate destination likely\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Vital signs\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Medically trained observations\u000d\u000a\u2022 In-person assessment can reassure that condition is not life-threatening\u000d\u000a\u2022 Higher chance of successful referral recommendation\u000d\u000a\u2022 May not have ambulance on scene if pt needs transport (fire truck)","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 64\u000d\u000aAMR (Field AMR)\u000d\u000a\u2022 BLS response initially requested by 911 dispatch\u000d\u000a\u2022 Paramedic / EMT on scene evaluated patient to be alternate destination\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Vital signs\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Medically trained observations\u000d\u000a\u2022 In-person assessment can reassure that condition is not life-threatening\u000d\u000a\u2022 Higher chance of successful referral recommendation\u000d\u000a\u2022 They are an ambulance on scene if pt needs transport","Identifying the Patient\u2019s Complaint\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 65\u000d\u000aPatient Interview\u000d\u000aWith telephonic interviewing, our diagnostic abilities are limited:\u000d\u000a\u2022 We rarely have objective data from diagnostic tools.\u000d\u000a\u2022 No direct exam / eyes on patient\u000d\u000a\u2022 No physical exam\u000d\u000a\u2022 We\u2019re asking objective questions about a subjective experience.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Relies on self-reporting / non-medically trained observations\u000d\u000a\u2022 Influenced heavily by caller/patient\u2019s state of mind\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Anxiety, Fear, Pain, Anger\u000d\u000aThe patient\u2019s phone signal may effect the quality of the call\u2026\u000d\u000aOur Signal\u000d\u000aTheir Signal\u000d\u000aor\u2026 or\u2026","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 66\u000d\u000aHow to Analyze Pain\u000d\u000aPAIN is what the patient says it is because:\u000d\u000a\u2022 It is the individual\u2019s experience\u000d\u000a\u2022 There aren\u2019t definitive diagnostic tools to measure it. \u000d\u000aThis is the #1 rule of 911 Nurse Navigation.\u000d\u000aQuestions\u000d\u000aWe use questions to probe where our eyes, fingers, and stethoscopes can\u2019t.\u000d\u000a\u2022 USE DISCRETION; we don\u2019t have to take everything a patient says at face value...\u000d\u000aAsk the patient to quantify their pain \u2013 0-10\u000d\u000aWhen did it start?\u000d\u000aHow does the patient describe it?\u000d\u000aArea, type, characteristics, & persistence\u000d\u000aHow would the patient evaluate it?\u000d\u000aWhat makes it better / worse?\u000d\u000aThe symptoms are what the \u000d\u000apatient says they are.","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 67\u000d\u000aExample: General Communication\u000d\u000aCaller GMR Patient Interview Questions\u000d\u000a\u201cI have a complaint of\u2026\u201d \u2022 Have you had these symptoms before?\u000d\u000a\u2022 Did you seek treatment?\u000d\u000a\u2022 What did you/they do about it?\u000d\u000a\u2022 Have you tried that this time?\u000d\u000aExample: Immobilization\u000d\u000aCaller GMR Patient Interview Questions\u000d\u000a\u201cI can\u2019t walk.\u201d \u2022 Are you incapable, or are you being limited by pain?\u000d\u000a\u2022 Are you too weak, or because you can\u2019t move your legs?\u000d\u000a\u2022 If you need to pee, can you make it to the bathroom?","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 68\u000d\u000aExample: Immobilization\u000d\u000aCaller GMR Patient Interview Questions\u000d\u000a\u201cMy head, neck, back,\u000d\u000aand stomach all hurt!\u201d\u000d\u000a\u2022 Which one started first?\u000d\u000a\u2022 Which hurts the worst?\u000d\u000a\u2022 Have you had these symptoms before?\u000d\u000a\u2022 Did you seek treatment?\u000d\u000a\u2022 What did you/they do about it?\u000d\u000a\u2022 Have you tried that this time?\u000d\u000a\u2022 Headache with HTN?\u000d\u000a\u2022 Numbness / tingling with diabetes?\u000d\u000a\u2022 Nausea / vomiting with a skipped period?\u000d\u000aWhat comorbidities \u000d\u000achange the complaint?","Exclusion List\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 69\u000d\u000aOverview\u000d\u000a911 Nurse Navigation is designed to help match low acuity patients with appropriate care. \u000d\u000aUnfortunately, there are a handful of patient situations, even when low acuity, that 911 NN \u000d\u000adoes not have the resources to help navigate. These situations have been compiled into an \u000d\u000aExclusion List.\u000d\u000aWhy do we have an Exclusion List?\u000d\u000aThe Exclusion List is part of the Call Flow process that is mapped out during contract \u000d\u000aimplementation. This foundation allows the contract to educate their call takers, and most of \u000d\u000athese calls are screened out before reaching 911 Nurse Navigation. Some exclusions will slip \u000d\u000athrough because:\u000d\u000a\u2022 The nurse is allowed to probe and get data that an EMD process may not reveal\u000d\u000a\u2022 Mistakes happen.\u000d\u000aWe are ALL Working \u000d\u000ato Help Our Patients\u000d\u000aWhen handed a call that we are not meant to \u000d\u000amanage, please handle it with calm, patience, and \u000d\u000ado not assume ill intent. \u000d\u000aAlways remember that you are a leader throughout \u000d\u000athe call. Guide it where it needs to go next. ","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 70\u000d\u000aExclusion \u000d\u000aScenarios \u000d\u000aLife threatening illness or injury\u000d\u000aIncarcerated / Arrested / Detained by Law Enforcement\u000d\u000aImpaired or unable to communicate due to drugs or alcohol \u000d\u000aPregnancy for a duration longer than 20 weeks\u000d\u000aHomicidal or Violent Intent\u000d\u000aNursing Home / SNF Patients \u000d\u000aThird-Party Callers\u000d\u000aIf the patient is directed to an ED by a clinical provider\u000d\u000aIf the patient is under the care of a medical professional at a facility\u000d\u000aIf the patient was directed to an ED by their residing facility\u2019s protocol ","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 71\u000d\u000aExclusion Workflows\u000d\u000aDuring Handoff\u000d\u000aScripting\u000d\u000aTell the dispatcher: \u000d\u000a\u201cUnfortunately, I cannot accept this call as this patient meets \u000d\u000a[exclusion criteria].\u201d \u000d\u000a\u2022 Be sure to cite the specific exclusion criteria that has been \u000d\u000amet.\u000d\u000aIf the dispatcher asks you what to do with the call and immediate life \u000d\u000athreat is not suspected, tell them to send the response they would have \u000d\u000asent if NN was unavailable.\u000d\u000a\u2022 If you suspect life-threatening illness or injury, request ALS.\u000d\u000aDocumentation\u000d\u000aWarm Transfer Do not document the call.\u000d\u000aCAD-to-CAD Cancel the call with reason, \u201cExclusion Criteria\u201d\u000d\u000aTracking fill out the \ud83d\udd17Feedback Form with the contract, \u000d\u000adate, and time of the call for tracking purposes.\u000d\u000a\u2022 We report repeated behaviors to the PSAPs \u000d\u000afor individual or systemic correction.","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 72\u000d\u000aAfter Handoff\u000d\u000aScripting\u000d\u000aOften, nurses will identify exclusion criteria during their \u000d\u000aassessment/triage. When this happens, please tell the patient:\u000d\u000a\u201cIt looks like we don\u2019t have any resources that match your current \u000d\u000asituation. I\u2019m going to contact dispatch and ask them to send you an \u000d\u000aambulance.\u201d\u000d\u000a\u2022 Also provide your normal ambulance instructions.\u000d\u000aNext Steps\u000d\u000a1. Warm Transfer to dispatch and tell them you were unable to \u000d\u000afinish assessing because the patient met exclusion criteria. \u000d\u000a\u27a2 Specify the exclusion criteria.\u000d\u000a\u27a2 If life-threat is suspected, request ALS for your patient.\u000d\u000aDocumentation\u000d\u000aWarm Transfer Finish documenting the call with the knowledge \u000d\u000ayou acquired prior to identifying the exclusion \u000d\u000acriteria and save as the type of ambulance \u000d\u000arequested.\u000d\u000aCAD-to-CAD \u2022 Put the exclusion criteria met in the \u000d\u000aComments.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Choose an appropriate ambulance type for \u000d\u000athe patient (ALS/BLS) and save.\u000d\u000a\u2022 RSC should only be chosen if the patient \u000d\u000astates they do not want an ambulance.\u000d\u000aTracking fill out the \ud83d\udd17Feedback Form with the contract, \u000d\u000adate, and time of the call for tracking purposes.\u000d\u000a\u2022 We report repeated behaviors to the PSAPs \u000d\u000afor individual or systemic correction.","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 73\u000d\u000aThe Seattle Exception\u000d\u000aGuidelines\u000d\u000aIf your Seattle patient\u2019s exclusion is life-threatening with the need for an ALS respons\u000d\u000aPlease request an ambulance through Seattle Fire.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Do this during or after handoff\u000d\u000aFor all other exclusions in Seattle\u000d\u000a1. NN will accept the patient\u000d\u000a2. Verify demographics and the basic patient situation\u000d\u000a3. Contact Seattle AMR to request an ambulance for their exclusion\u000d\u000a4. Triage not Complete patient.\u000d\u000aBecause Seattle processes \u000d\u000atheir calls a little differently, \u000d\u000awe process their exclusions \u000d\u000aa little differently!","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 74\u000d\u000aExclusion Criteria Examples & Workflows\u000d\u000aExample 1: Life-Threatening Indicators\u000d\u000aExclusion Identified\u000d\u000aThe patient\u2019s hemodynamic status is suspected to \u000d\u000abe compromised, and the patient\u2019s life could be \u000d\u000ain danger without quick, on-scene assessment \u000d\u000aand intervention.\u000d\u000aHow Do We Know?\u000d\u000aTerms like \"Shortness of Breath\" and \"Chest \u000d\u000aPain\" rightfully cause concern for most clinicians. \u000d\u000aThey also have a wide range \u000d\u000aof subjectivity. Follow the ABCs and be vigilant \u000d\u000awhen clinical data points to life-threating \u000d\u000asymptoms.\u000d\u000aUse Your Clinical \u000d\u000aJudgement!\u000d\u000aGather Additional Data When Needed\u000d\u000a\u2022 Unconscious or sudden, unexplained change in neuro status\u000d\u000a\u2022 Unable to complete sentences due to respiratory distress or audible wheezing\u000d\u000a\u2022 Hemorrhage: uncontrolled and/or uncontrollable bleeding. \u201cSpurting\u201d\u000d\u000a\u2022 Chest Pain / MI: may radiate to arms, jaw, abdomen, present with feelings of anxiety\u000d\u000a/ dread, feeling of something heavy on chest, diaphoresis, dizziness, or weakness.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Stroke: B.E.F.A.S.T. \u2013 Balance Loss, Eyes (Vision changes), Facial Droop, Arm \u000d\u000aWeakness, Speech Difficulty, Time to Call 911\u000d\u000aWhy Exclude? \u000d\u000aTime to care is of the essence for these patients and non-EMS resources (clinics, virtual care, \u000d\u000arideshare drivers, etc.) aren\u2019t equipped to handle medical emergencies.","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 75\u000d\u000aExample 2: Incarceration\u000d\u000aExclusion Identified\u000d\u000aThe patient is currently in the custody of law \u000d\u000aenforcement personnel. This could be someone that\u2019s \u000d\u000abeen arrested and is handcuffed on the sidewalk, or it \u000d\u000acould be a call from inside a jail or detention center.\u000d\u000aThis One Is \u000d\u000aStraight Forward \u000d\u000aHow Do We Know?\u000d\u000aTypically, the officer or staff member of the \u000d\u000acorrectional facility will identify themselves and the \u000d\u000asituation. If there\u2019s any doubt, ask the officer / nurse \u000d\u000aif the patient is currently in custody or under arrest.\u000d\u000aWhy Exclude? \u000d\u000aLaw enforcement has strict protocols for handling medical needs for those in their care, and \u000d\u000aCCRs are ill-equipped to handle the extra oversight and security considerations needed for \u000d\u000apatients in custody. Rideshare is not an option!","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 76\u000d\u000aExample 3: Drugs or Alcohol Impairment\u000d\u000aExclusion Identified\u000d\u000aThe key here is Impairment. \u000d\u000a\u2022 The patient shows signs / symptoms of diminished LOC.\u000d\u000aHow Do We Know?\u000d\u000aDon\u2019t focus on the substance consumed or the amount taken:\u000d\u000a\u2022 A 120 lb patient that never drinks and a 250 lb alcoholic \u000d\u000aget impaired at very different quantities\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Focus on clinical signs/symptoms\u000d\u000a\u2022 Slurred or rapid speech\u000d\u000a\u2022 Disorderly thought processes\u000d\u000a\u2022 Slow to react to questions\u000d\u000a\u2022 Reports of uncoordinated balance/movement\u000d\u000a\u2022 Ask Standard LOC questions\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Day of week, time of day, location, President, et.\u000d\u000aAssess To \u000d\u000aDetermine\u000d\u000aImpairment!\u000d\u000aWhy Exclude? \u000d\u000aIf a patient is suspected to be impaired, their ability to consent to and follow-up on \u000d\u000atreatment is compromised. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Additionally, these patients are best served by specialized resources and/or \u000d\u000atreatments that are not available at standard walk-in clinics.","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 77\u000d\u000aExample 4: Pregnant > 20 weeks\u000d\u000aA Straight-Forward Scenario\u000d\u000aExclusion Identified\u000d\u000aAs soon as you find out a patient is pregnant, verify how far along they are.\u000d\u000aHow Do We Know?\u000d\u000aTypically, the officer or staff member of the correctional facility will identify themselves and \u000d\u000athe situation. If there\u2019s any doubt, ask the officer / nurse if the patient is currently in custody \u000d\u000aor under arrest.\u000d\u000aWhy Exclude? \u000d\u000aAlmost any complaint from a patient >20 weeks pregnant will also include a wellness check \u000d\u000aon the baby. This generally requires specialty resources only available at Obstetric clinics and \u000d\u000ahospitals.","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 78\u000d\u000aExample 5: Homicidal or Violent intent\u000d\u000aExclusion Identified\u000d\u000aThe patient has taken actions, or is threatening /\u000d\u000aconsidering taking actions, that will harm themselves or \u000d\u000aothers.\u000d\u000aHow Do We Know?\u000d\u000aTriggering this exclusion requires more than ideation. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Consider if the patient has a plan, the means, and \u000d\u000aintent to commit harm. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Are the thoughts of doing harm fleeting or \u000d\u000aconsistent? \u000d\u000a\u2022 Passive or active? \u000d\u000a\u2022 Controllable or overwhelming? \u000d\u000a\u2022 Are voices or other hallucinations involved?\u000d\u000aUse Clinical \u000d\u000aJudgement\u000d\u000aWhy Exclude? \u000d\u000aSomeone who is actively a threat to themselves or others need resources to ensure scene, \u000d\u000apatient, and first responder safety. Community Care Resources (CCRs) that don\u2019t specialize in \u000d\u000aBehavioral/Mental Health (BMH), and all known rideshare services, do not have these \u000d\u000acapabilities.","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 79\u000d\u000aExample 6: Nursing Home/SNF Patients\u000d\u000aIdentify The Facility\u000d\u000aExclusion Identified\u000d\u000aPatients in a full-time care facility with medical direction.\u000d\u000aHow Do We Know?\u000d\u000aIf the caller / patient doesn\u2019t identify the facility as a Nursing Home or Skilled Nursing Facility \u000d\u000a(SNF), you can Google the facility and see from there. \u000d\u000a\u2022 This exclusion specifically targets full-time care facilities with on-site medical staff.\u000d\u000a\u2022 This exclusion does not apply to Assisted Living.\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Assisted Living homes are not full-time care facilities, and residents can\u000d\u000atypically come and go as they please.\u000d\u000aWhy Exclude? \u000d\u000aResidents of these facilities are under the care of medically trained staff with medical \u000d\u000adirection. When they call for an ambulance, it is typically via physician\u2019s direction \u2013 either \u000d\u000adirectly or by standing order/protocol.","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 80\u000d\u000aExample 7: Third Party Callers\u000d\u000aExclusion Identified\u000d\u000aTechnically speaking, a third-party call is when an \u000d\u000aincoming call comes from someone who is not on-site \u000d\u000awith the patient. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Typically, these are via alarm companies (like \u000d\u000aLifeAlert) or family members who called 911 on \u000d\u000aa relative\u2019s behalf after a phone conversation \u000d\u000awith the patient.\u000d\u000aInternally, we also use this designation for calls where \u000d\u000athe patient is unable to answer our questions and the \u000d\u000acaller (typically a bystander, staff member, or friend) is \u000d\u000aunable to provide meaningful data on the patient or \u000d\u000atheir condition.\u000d\u000aHow Do We Know?\u000d\u000aIf the patient and the caller are unable to supply \u000d\u000ainformation about the patient and their current \u000d\u000acondition, we won\u2019t be able to adequately triage and \u000d\u000aobtain an accurate NMTARA level for safe patient care.\u000d\u000aAlways Ask to \u000d\u000aSpeak to the \u000d\u000aPatient!\u000d\u000aWhy Exclude? \u000d\u000aOur clinical pathways require a willing and knowledgeable participant to give answers to \u000d\u000aspecific questions. Without someone on-site who can assist us to obtain up-to-date answers, \u000d\u000aour NMTARA accuracy and patient safety may be compromised.","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 81\u000d\u000aExample 8: Physician Directive\u000d\u000aExclusion Identified\u000d\u000aSome patients or care givers have already spoken to a \u000d\u000aphysician prior to calling 911 \u2013 either via phone, by being \u000d\u000aunder their direct care, or by facility protocol.\u000d\u000aHow Do We Know?\u000d\u000aGenerally, the patient or caregiver will tell you they\u2019ve \u000d\u000aalready called the doctor and have been advised to go to \u000d\u000athe hospital. \u000d\u000aIf the patient\u2019s symptoms aren\u2019t life-threatening, and if the \u000d\u000apatient agrees to it, we can use our clinical pathways to \u000d\u000afind out if we can safely transport the patient via Rideshare \u000d\u000ato save them from an expensive ambulance bill.\u000d\u000aDoctor\u2019s \u000d\u000aOrders\u000d\u000aWhy Exclude? \u000d\u000aWhen patients have consulted providers who instructed them to report to an ED, or when a \u000d\u000acaretaker is following standing protocols to escalate care through 911, Nurse Navigation is \u000d\u000aunlikely to provide an agreeable solution outside of that guidance. As nurses, we help enact \u000d\u000aphysicians\u2019 directives when it is possible within our scope of practice.","Leading with Empathy\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 82\u000d\u000aThe Cornerstones of Empathy\u000d\u000aActive Listening\u000d\u000aListen to understand, not respond. \u000d\u000aThink about how they are feeling as \u000d\u000athey describe their situation. For \u000d\u000aexample \u201cthat must be frustrating\u201d or \u000d\u000a\u201cThat sounds painful\u201d to acknowledge \u000d\u000athe caller\u2019s concerns.\u000d\u000aAvoid Assumptions\u000d\u000aAssumptions lead to unconscious \u000d\u000abias which can inhibit equitable and \u000d\u000acompassionate care. Approach each \u000d\u000apatient as an individual with unique \u000d\u000aexperiences, beliefs, and concerns.\u000d\u000aOffer Comfort\u000d\u000aWhile we cannot hold our patient\u2019s \u000d\u000ahand, we can still tell them that we are \u000d\u000asorry they aren\u2019t feeling well and they \u000d\u000awe are committed to getting them care \u000d\u000aquickly.\u000d\u000aAvoid Burnout\u000d\u000aTake care of your own well-being. \u000d\u000aMaintaining a self-care routine can \u000d\u000amotivate you to provide quality \u000d\u000apatient care. Nurses need to be \u000d\u000aemotionally and mentally available \u000d\u000ato advocate for their patients\u000d\u000aHow Empathy Benefits our Patients\u000d\u000aReduce Patient \u000d\u000aDistress\u000d\u000aHigher Patient \u000d\u000aSatisfaction\u000d\u000aPrevents \u000d\u000aEmotional Harm\u000d\u000aIncreased \u000d\u000aEfficiency\u000d\u000aPatients who are \u000d\u000aanxious or scared \u000d\u000abelieve they are having \u000d\u000aan emergency. \u000d\u000aRecognizing this and \u000d\u000aresponding with \u000d\u000aempathy can greatly \u000d\u000areduce their distress and \u000d\u000aanxiety.\u000d\u000aEmpathy leads to more \u000d\u000apositive patient \u000d\u000aexperiences. Patients \u000d\u000areport higher \u000d\u000asatisfaction scores when \u000d\u000athey feel that someone \u000d\u000acares.\u000d\u000aEmpathy helps validate \u000d\u000aemotions, prevent \u000d\u000amisunderstandings, and \u000d\u000areduce feelings of \u000d\u000aisolation.\u000d\u000aNurses are more likely to \u000d\u000asuccessfully navigate \u000d\u000apatients to a clinic or \u000d\u000aother alternate \u000d\u000adestination","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 83\u000d\u000aEmpathy Phrases\u000d\u000aAcknowledgment Encouragement Validation\u000d\u000a\"I can see that this is really \u000d\u000adistressing for you right now; \u000d\u000aI\u2019m here to help.\"\u000d\u000a\"You\u2019re doing great by \u000d\u000areaching out; it\u2019s a big step \u000d\u000ato ask for help.\"\u000d\u000a\"Your feelings are valid, and \u000d\u000ait\u2019s important that we \u000d\u000aaddress your concerns.\"\u000d\u000a\"It sounds like you're going \u000d\u000athrough a tough time, and it\u2019s \u000d\u000acompletely understandable to \u000d\u000afeel this way.\"\u000d\u000a\"You\u2019re taking the right \u000d\u000aaction by calling us; we\u2019ll \u000d\u000afigure this out together.\"\u000d\u000a\"It\u2019s completely normal to \u000d\u000afeel anxious in situations like \u000d\u000athis; let\u2019s see how we can \u000d\u000ahelp.\"\u000d\u000a\"I can see that this is really \u000d\u000adistressing for you right now; \u000d\u000aI\u2019m here to help. How long \u000d\u000ahave you been feeling this \u000d\u000away?\"\u000d\u000a\"I understand that this \u000d\u000asituation is very frustrating, \u000d\u000aand it\u2019s okay to feel \u000d\u000aoverwhelmed. Let\u2019s talk \u000d\u000aabout what\u2019s been \u000d\u000ahappening and see how we \u000d\u000acan assist you.\"\u000d\u000a\"That sounds really difficult; I \u000d\u000aunderstand how concerning \u000d\u000athis must be for you. Can you \u000d\u000atell me more about what \u000d\u000ayou\u2019re experiencing?\"\u000d\u000aClarifying Intentions Reassurance Supportive Promises\u000d\u000a\"My goal is to ensure you get \u000d\u000athe best care possible; let\u2019s \u000d\u000atalk about what\u2019s happening.\"\u000d\u000a\"I\u2019m here to listen and \u000d\u000asupport you. We\u2019ll work \u000d\u000athrough this together.\"\u000d\u000a\"I will do my best to assist \u000d\u000ayou and get you the help you \u000d\u000aneed.\"\u000d\u000a\"I want to make sure we \u000d\u000aunderstand your situation \u000d\u000afully, so we can provide the \u000d\u000aright support.\"\u000d\u000a\"You\u2019re not alone in this; I\u2019m \u000d\u000ahere to help you get the \u000d\u000acare you need.\"\u000d\u000a\"Let\u2019s take this step by step; \u000d\u000aI\u2019m here with you \u000d\u000athroughout this process.\"\u000d\u000a\u201cRight now, you are my \u000d\u000apriority. Take the time you \u000d\u000aneed.\u201d\u000d\u000a\u201cYou did the right thing in \u000d\u000acalling us.\u201d\u000d\u000a\u201cI\u2019m going to talk you \u000d\u000athrough this, but please let \u000d\u000ame know if you have any \u000d\u000aquestions along the way. \u000d\u000aREMEMBER: Your patient may be perceiving a life-threatening emergency, so they are not \u000d\u000ahaving a good day. Your job is to assess the situation and provide reassurance and empathy \u000d\u000awhile navigating them to an appropriate care destination. \u000d\u000aYour patient is more likely to agree to navigation if they feel heard and cared for.","De-Escalation\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 84\u000d\u000aWhy does it matter to de-escalate?\u000d\u000a\u2022 Callers who are in crisis cannot think clearly and make decisions even when a nurse is \u000d\u000aproviding a reasonable solution to their problem.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Prevents unnecessary emergency utilization: Proper education and assessment can avoid \u000d\u000aoveruse of 911 and ER resources.\u000d\u000a\u2022 The patient's expectations are based on their limited knowledge and understanding of \u000d\u000athe program.\u000d\u000aCore Concepts\u000d\u000aEmpathy\u000d\u000aActive Listening\u000d\u000aValidation\u000d\u000aClear Communication\u000d\u000aSet Expectations\u000d\u000aPrioritize Safety","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 85\u000d\u000aRemain Calm\u000d\u000a\u2022 Be calm and composed, this isn't about you.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Use a softer, reassuring tone, avoid raising your voice.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Avoid arguing or dismissive concerns, promote a safe space.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Ask open ended questions with slow, deliberate speech.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Breathe deeply to maintain your own composure.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Maintain a professional, compassionate demeanor regardless of caller behavior.","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 86\u000d\u000aValidate what the Caller is Saying\u000d\u000a\u2022 Show genuine interest and focus on the patient\u2019s words.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Maintain a respectful attitude.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Acknowledge feelings without judgment.\u000d\u000a\u2022 If you actively listen, you can demonstrate they are understood.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Listen with the intention of understanding instead of arguing.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Repeat back what the patient says in a different way.\u000d\u000aGet the Caller to Participate\u000d\u000aSpeak to the patient as you would a good friend or family member.\u000d\u000a\"Let\u2019s take a moment to \u000d\u000abreathe together.\"\u000d\u000a\"Let's focus on one \u000d\u000astep at a time.\"\u000d\u000a\u201cCan you tell me what you see \u000d\u000aaround you? What\u2019s something \u000d\u000ayou can focus on right now?\"\u000d\u000a\u201cCan you tell me what you see \u000d\u000aaround you? What\u2019s something \u000d\u000ayou can focus on right now?\"","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 87\u000d\u000aSet & Manage Expectations\u000d\u000aTransparency is key:\u000d\u000a\u2022 This includes the scope of 911 Nurse Navigation. \u000d\u000a\u27a2 Explain the purpose of 911 Nurse Navigation and what the caller can expect.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Inform them about available resources and support systems.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Involve the patient in developing a plan, confirm they are on board.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Provide education surrounding the plan. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Allow patient to write call back number down.\u000d\u000a\u201cWould you like me to go \u000d\u000aover anything we\u2019ve \u000d\u000atalked about so far?\u201d","Conversation Guide\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 88\u000d\u000aThis conversation guide training reconceptualizes the call flow of the 911 Nurse Navigator by \u000d\u000achunking the call into segments for easy recall. While there are talking point requirements, this \u000d\u000aconversation guide is not meant to be a script, but a reminder of what to say and when.\u000d\u000aCall Overview\u000d\u000aReference Quick Links\u000d\u000aInfo & Suggested Scripting Barriers\u000d\u000a1 About Call Handoffs\u000d\u000a View View\u000d\u000a2 Greeting the Caller View View\u000d\u000a3 Verify Patient Details View View\u000d\u000a4 Clinical Discovery View View\u000d\u000a5 Clinical Pathway View View\u000d\u000a6 Care Suggestions View View\u000d\u000a7 Plan of Care View View\u000d\u000a8 Arrange Care View\u000d\u000a9 Partner Contact View\u000d\u000aFor post-call activities, please see the Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ), Dispositions and\u000d\u000aDocumentation Do\u2019s & Don\u2019ts sections of this reference guide. ","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 89\u000d\u000aAbout Call Handoffs\u000d\u000aHandoff of the patient from the 911 system (911 operator or Field Staff) to 911 Nurse \u000d\u000aNavigation. Assume the patient is on the line (or on speaker phone), listening to the interaction. \u000d\u000aThis handoff should be short, professional, and instill confidence in the patient and 911 partner \u000d\u000athat they are in good hands.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Listen for the whisper\u000d\u000a\u27a2 It tells you where the call is from and if the contract has CAD-to-CAD\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Reminds you to use the appropriate greeting for the contract.\u000d\u000aCall Handoff Types\u000d\u000a911 Dispatcher CAD \u2013 CAD Field\u000d\u000a1. Incident address\u000d\u000a2. Phone number\u000d\u000a3. Brief situation\u000d\u000aAccept calls without \u000d\u000aexcessive delay\u000d\u000a1. Incident address\u000d\u000a1. Incident address\u000d\u000a2. Brief situation\u000d\u000a3. Patient vital signs\u000d\u000aFLD=Field Fire\u000d\u000aAMR=Field AMR\u000d\u000aCall Greetings \u000d\u000ashould match our \u000d\u000acontracts and \u000d\u000ainclude the nurse\u2019s \u000d\u000aidentification. ","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 90\u000d\u000aCall Handoff Information Exchange\u000d\u000aPush\u000d\u000aInfo given to 911 Nurse Navigation by dispatcher / EMS\u000d\u000a\u2022 Should include the \u201cexpected\u201d info for call type\u000d\u000a\u2022 May be more than \u201cexpected\u201d info \u2013 reference \u000d\u000anumber, patient name, etc.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Document reference numbers when given\u000d\u000aPull\u000d\u000aInfo requested by 911 Nurse Navigation from dispatcher / EMS\u000d\u000a\u2022 Only pull \u201cexpected data\u201d when it is not being offered \u000d\u000aby dispatcher / EMS\u000d\u000a\u2022 Do not pull info outside of the \u201cexpected data\u201d \u000d\u000a\u2022 It is okay to clarify any pushed data\u000d\u000aQuick handoffs allow 911 dispatch to resume answering calls while we to \u000d\u000atake care of the patient. It shows we are competent, efficient, and \u000d\u000aconfirms the patient is in good hands.","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 91\u000d\u000aGreeting the Caller\u000d\u000aThis greeting explains why the caller/patient is \u000d\u000atalking to a nurse. Include required talking \u000d\u000apoints but make it your own. This statement \u000d\u000aconveys empathy and explains to the patient \u000d\u000awhy they are speaking with a nurse.\u000d\u000aThis reduces confusion, increases \u000d\u000aunderstanding and buy in, and allows the \u000d\u000apatient an opportunity to opt out.\u000d\u000aRequired Introduction Verbiage \u000d\u000a\u201cHi, my name is \u000d\u000a[name]. I\u2019m a \u000d\u000anurse on a \u000d\u000arecorded line.\u201d\u000d\u000aUse this greeting with every new person \u000d\u000ayou talk to throughout the call.","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 92\u000d\u000aDO\u000d\u000aSet expectations with the required talking points: \u000d\u000a\u2713 Reintroduce yourself \u000d\u000a\u2713 Recorded call disclosure\u000d\u000a\u2713 Contract Name\u000d\u000a\u2713 No ambulance is on the way at this time\u000d\u000a\u2713 Explain why they are speaking with a nurse\u000d\u000aDON\u2019T\u000d\u000a\u00d7 Say \u201cYou don\u2019t qualify for an ambulance.\u201d\u000d\u000a\u00d7 Say \u201cIt\u2019s going to be a long wait\u201d \u000d\u000a(or specify several hours of wait time)\u000d\u000a\u00d7 \u201cEMS is backed up or no ambulances available in your area\u201d\u000d\u000a\u00d7 \u201cThis is not an emergency\u201d","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 93\u000d\u000aVerify Patient Details\u000d\u000aVerify the patients identify by asking 3 data points:\u000d\u000aFirst and Last Name Date of Birth Phone Number\u000d\u000aConfirm the spelling of the patient\u2019s name!\u000d\u000aOther Data Points\u000d\u000aExample: Patient Verification Verbiage \u000d\u000a\u201cFor your security, please verify your full name, date of birth, and phone number. Is that \u000d\u000athe traditional spelling?\u201d\u000d\u000aAge & Gender\u000d\u000aCare recommendations, diagnosis, and patient education are more precise\u000d\u000aInsurance Type \u000d\u000aShould be collected for all patients to match with the best care options, allow 911 Nurse \u000d\u000aNavigation to trend resource usage, and explore service gaps with our contracts / partners.","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 94\u000d\u000aClinical Discovery\u000d\u000aAsk probing questions to understand their chief \u000d\u000acomplaint, allowing you to match the patient with the \u000d\u000amost appropriate protocol, resulting in a more \u000d\u000aaccurate NMTARA level.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Your goal is to gather enough relevant \u000d\u000ainformation to be confident in the pathway. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Primary source-data from the patient is priority. \u000d\u000a\u27a2 Always ask to speak with the patient \u000d\u000aunless inappropriate (i.e. age, \u000d\u000adevelopmental level, aphasic, etc).\u000d\u000aAssess patient responses using your best judgement and \u000d\u000aimmediately escalate to an ALS response if needed.\u000d\u000aUse OLDCARTS or another \u000d\u000amnemonic to guide your probing:\u000d\u000aO Onset\u000d\u000aL Location\u000d\u000aD Duration\u000d\u000aC Characteristics\u000d\u000aA Aggravating / Alleviating factors\u000d\u000aR Radiation\u000d\u000aT Timing\u000d\u000aS Severity \u000d\u000aExample: Clinical Discovery\u000d\u000a\u201cTell me more about your \u000d\u000a[condition]. When did it start and \u000d\u000ahas it been treated?\u201d\u000d\u000aExample: Defining Pain\u000d\u000a\u201cDescribe your pain. Does it \u000d\u000afeel sharp and stabby or dull \u000d\u000aand achy?\u201d","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 95\u000d\u000aClinical Pathway\u000d\u000aFollow the clinical pathway to completion. These consist of MD-approved questions. \u000d\u000aClinical protocols are NOT optional. Think of them as your failsafe. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Ask all questions to ensure you reach an accurate NMTARA level. \u000d\u000a\u27a2 Nurses can always escalate care with a reasonable concern, but NMTARA can\u2019t \u000d\u000abe downgraded. \u000d\u000a\u2022 If you believe the NMTARA level is falsely high, report it so we can track and work on \u000d\u000asystem solutions.\u000d\u000aVerbiage\u000d\u000aKeep the caller / patient talking and informed \u000d\u000aof next steps, once determined.\u000d\u000aClinical protocols are followed to the end; All questions asked \u000d\u000aor confirmed. All steps completed.","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 96\u000d\u000aCare Suggestions\u000d\u000aConsider the patient\u2019s circumstances and resource availability. A hierarchy of choices will be \u000d\u000apresented to you. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Select the closest match to the NMTARA level (i.e., REF or VC for NMTARA 1-5)\u000d\u000a\u2022 For your consideration:\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Does insurance play a factor?\u000d\u000ao Clinics, specialty resources, Kaiser, etc\u2026?\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Will they potentially need imaging or lab services? \u000d\u000a\u27a2 What care resources are available for their area?\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Does the patient have mobility restrictions? \u000d\u000a\u27a2 Can the patient be safely transported in a rideshare?\u000d\u000aIf any of these options limit your choices, document it! \u000d\u000aExample: Urgent Care Referral\u000d\u000a\u201cBased on your answers, I think \u000d\u000agoing to a nearby urgent care clinic \u000d\u000awill be best for what\u2019s going on \u000d\u000awith you today. Do you need me to \u000d\u000aarrange a ride for you?\u201d","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 97\u000d\u000aExample: Virtual Care Referral \u000d\u000a\u201cBased on your answers and your \u000d\u000ainsurance, I recommend seeing a virtual \u000d\u000aurgent care provider for your issue. You\u2019ll \u000d\u000aspeak with the intake coordinator before \u000d\u000ayou are connected to the provider.\u201d\u000d\u000aExample: Virtual Care Provider Explanation \u000d\u000a\u201cWe have a Doctor / Provider here you can speak with \u000d\u000aso you don\u2019t have to leave the comfort of your own \u000d\u000ahome. We have ER and Urgent Care doctors that can \u000d\u000aprescribe medications and send them to whichever \u000d\u000apharmacy you choose. We would also provide the ride \u000d\u000athere, and back, when the medication is ready for \u000d\u000apickup.\u201d\u000d\u000aExample: EMS Transport \u000d\u000a\u201cBecause you cannot safely enter or operate \u000d\u000aa vehicle at this time, I will arrange an \u000d\u000aambulance to take you to the ER.\u201d","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 98\u000d\u000aPlan of Care\u000d\u000aThe patient must be informed of what their plan of care is. This \u000d\u000aincludes verbal consent to the plan. Summarize the call and actions \u000d\u000ataken to ensure the patient has a clear understanding of next steps: \u000d\u000a\u2022 Where they are going?\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Clinic or hospital name and address.\u000d\u000a\u2022 How will they get there?\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Rideshare, ambulance, or private vehicle.\u000d\u000a\u2022 What should they take with them?\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Photo ID and insurance care; the clinic may also collect a co-pay.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Who to call when the plan breaks or they need a ride home?\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Provide the patient call back number and explain what it\u2019s for.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Home care instructions?\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Documenting only what was verbalized.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Will there be a follow-up call or communications?\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Follow up to get their thoughts and feedback regarding the care they received.\u000d\u000aThe patient should be aware of the specifics regarding the \u000d\u000aplan of care and they know who to call if the plan breaks.","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 99\u000d\u000aExample: Virtual Care Plan\u000d\u000a\u201cBased on your symptoms, we determined that virtual care is the \u000d\u000abest care option for your sore throat. I am going to conference in a \u000d\u000acare coordinator. They will ask you to verify your information, like I \u000d\u000adid, and collect your insurance information as well - similar to an \u000d\u000ain-person clinic visit. After that, they will connect you with a \u000d\u000aprovider. We want to make sure we met your expectations. Keep an \u000d\u000aeye out for a call from us in the next couple of days; we\u2019d love to \u000d\u000ahear your feedback.\u201d","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 100\u000d\u000aExample: Transportation \u000d\u000a\u201cI have arranged a ride to pick you up in \u000d\u000a5 minutes to take you to [clinic name] \u000d\u000alocated at [clinic location]. [Driver \u000d\u000aname] will pick you up in a blue Honda. \u000d\u000aI\u2019ve told them you are wearing a red \u000d\u000ajacket and blue jeans. Please take down \u000d\u000athis phone number so you can give us a \u000d\u000acall when you are done at [clinic name] \u000d\u000aand we will get you back home. We will \u000d\u000afollow up with you tomorrow to conduct \u000d\u000aa survey about your experience with \u000d\u000a911 Nurse Navigation.\u201d","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 101\u000d\u000aArrange Care\u000d\u000aThe nurse arranges care agreed upon by the patient. Ensure the patient understands the plan \u000d\u000aof care and who to contact if the plan breaks. The patient has the chance to ask questions and \u000d\u000adecline before care is arranged.\u000d\u000aExamples of Care Options\u000d\u000a\u2022 Select an open clinic and verify they accept the patient\u2019s insurance\u000d\u000a\u2022 Arrange transport to a community care resource\u000d\u000a\u2022 Conference RelyMD for a virtual care visit\u000d\u000a\u2022 Correctly activate an ambulance response based on contract directions\u000d\u000aExample: Virtual Care Next Steps \u000d\u000a\u201cLet\u2019s recap your call to 911 Nurse \u000d\u000aNavigation, your initial complaint was \u000d\u000a[xyz] and based on the assessment, we \u000d\u000aagreed that a virtual care visit is our next \u000d\u000astep. Please take down this phone number \u000d\u000ain case you can\u2019t complete your virtual \u000d\u000acare visit or if you have any issues. You \u000d\u000amay hear silence followed by a brief hold \u000d\u000aas I get that set up for you. You will answer \u000d\u000asome questions with the care coordinator \u000d\u000abefore speaking with the provider.\u201d","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 102\u000d\u000aPartner Contact\u000d\u000aWhen calling any partner (dispatch, VC, Crisis Connections, etc.) always:\u000d\u000a\u2022 Identify yourself\u000d\u000a\u2022 Who you work for\u000d\u000a\u2022 Why you are calling\u000d\u000aExample: Ambulance Request \u000d\u000a\u201cThis is [name] with 911 Nurse \u000d\u000aNavigation. I\u2019m calling for an ambulance \u000d\u000afor [address] due to [patient condition, \u000d\u000arefusal of resources, limited mobility, \u000d\u000aetc]\u201d.\u000d\u000aExample: Virtual Care Request \u000d\u000a\u201cThis is [name] with 911 Nurse \u000d\u000aNavigation. I have a patient in need of \u000d\u000avirtual urgent care.\u201d","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 103\u000d\u000aVirtual Care-RelyMD Process \u000d\u000a1 Check the VC exclusion list before proceeding\u000d\u000a2 Explain the RelyMD process to the patient (set expectations) \u000d\u000a3 Follow Corti to arrange care.","Potential Call Barriers \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 104\u000d\u000aCall Handoff\u000d\u000aThe dispatcher has cross streets, but no specific address.\u000d\u000aEnter the cross streets into Google maps (i.e. \u201cintersection of 7th and Main \u000d\u000a(city/state)\u201d). Ask the patient to describe what they see around them and \u000d\u000acorrelate with information from maps.\u000d\u000aThe nurse is having trouble geolocating the address in Logis.\u000d\u000aDon\u2019t geolocate here. Wait until you are on with the patient to clarify address \u000d\u000aand geolocate.\u000d\u000aThe patient is yelling / belligerent during the handoff.\u000d\u000aWait until the patient stops talking and offer empathy, provide context, and \u000d\u000apreview next steps as needed. \u000d\u000aThe nurse continues to ask dispatch for excessive information \u000d\u000aOnly ask clarifying questions. All other information can be confirmed with the \u000d\u000apatient / caller, including geolocation for addresses","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 105\u000d\u000aGreeting the Caller\u000d\u000aThe caller / patient interrupts and demands an ambulance \u000d\u000aWait until the patient stops talking and offer empathy and a \u2018why\u2019:\u000d\u000a\u2022 \u201cI\u2019m sorry you\u2019re not feeling well today. I\u2019m a nurse and I am here to \u000d\u000aget you the help you need today.\u201d\u000d\u000aThe caller / patient does not speak English\u000d\u000aConference in the language line services; see Corti for instructions\u000d\u000aThe patient refuses to speak on a recorded line\u000d\u000aExplain that we record for quality assurance. if they still refuse, end the call \u000d\u000aand send it back for BLS.\u000d\u000a\u2022 \u201cI\u2019m sorry. I cannot proceed with this call. I will have an ambulance \u000d\u000asent to your location.\u000d\u000aWhile on the phone, our tone can cause both \u000d\u000aintentional and unintentional emotional ripples \u000d\u000athroughout a conversation. Even our physical \u000d\u000afacial expression has a subtle, but meaningful, \u000d\u000aimpact on our tone, and therefore, the other \u000d\u000aparty\u2019s willingness to participate. \u000d\u000aWe should always aim to \u000d\u000aacknowledge, respect, and \u000d\u000arespond to the emotional \u000d\u000aenvironment of the room. ","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 106\u000d\u000aPatient Verification\u000d\u000aThe patient refuses to verify demographic information\u000d\u000aTake what information you can and explain the purpose of your request.\u000d\u000aThe patient identifies as non-binary\u000d\u000aRespectfully explain that some questions are included or excluded based on \u000d\u000abiological sex so that we can best match them to the proper care.\u000d\u000aThe patient has a 911 only phone\u000d\u000aAsk the patient / caller to confirm if it\u2019s 911 only. If so, put \u2018911 only\u2019 in the \u000d\u000anumber field. If the patient / caller has no phone, put \u2018no phone\u2019 or \u000d\u000a\u2018unknown\u2019 in the number field","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 107\u000d\u000aClinical Discovery\u000d\u000aThe patient reports red-flag symptoms\u000d\u000aBased on your nursing judgement, immediately escalate care to an ALS \u000d\u000aresponse, if needed, in the event of:\u000d\u000a\u2022 New onset of weakness\u000d\u000a\u2022 Persistent or worsening pain that interferes with activity\u000d\u000a\u2022 New onset of confusion or cognitive issues\u000d\u000a\u2022 Continuous vomiting / diarrhea\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Especially in the very young and very old\u000d\u000a\u2022 Difficulty breathing\u000d\u000a\u27a2 With or without blue lips, mouth, or tongue\u000d\u000a\u2022 Chest pain/pressure that radiates up to jaw or down arm\u000d\u000aThe caller is providing answers for patient without consult\u000d\u000aAsk to speak directly with the patient if possible ","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 108\u000d\u000aClinical Pathway\u000d\u000aThe patient\u2019s reply indicates they misunderstood of the question\u000d\u000a\u2022 If they don\u2019t understand the question as written, rephrase to ask the \u000d\u000aspirit of the question\u000d\u000a\u2022 \u2018And\u2019 and \u2018Or\u2019 are very important aspects of the question and should \u000d\u000anot be omitted\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Example: (Age 50+) Is there a tearing or ripping pain, or is the \u000d\u000apain rapidly getting worse?\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Example: Are (you/they) having persistent nausea and \u000d\u000avomiting?\u000d\u000aThe patient gives vague answers\u000d\u000a\u2022 Ask the patient to clarify their answer if needed (i.e., \u201cWhen you say \u000d\u000asometimes, does that mean right now?\u201d)\u000d\u000a\u2022 Ask for a concrete \u2018Yes\u2019 or \u2018No\u2019 answer\u000d\u000a\u2022 Ensure that your click matches the patient\u2019s answer\u000d\u000aData Collection Issues\u000d\u000a\u2022 System glitches\u000d\u000a\u2022 Refresh system [Log out and log back in]\u000d\u000a\u2022 Use Briggs book if Corti is not functional\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Need backup for contract routing\u000d\u000a\u2022 Report pathway issues to Nathan-if questions don\u2019t make sense or \u000d\u000aunable to move forward. ","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 109\u000d\u000aCare Suggestions\u000d\u000aThe clinic is closed or doesn\u2019t take the patient\u2019s insurance\u000d\u000a\u2022 Place the caller on hold and call the clinic to verify their hours and \u000d\u000aaccepted insurance\u000d\u000aThere are no providers available\u000d\u000aPivot and offer the patient a ride to a clinic\u000d\u000aThe patient demands an ambulance and refuses other resources\u000d\u000aDe-escalate and explain that a clinic or virtual care visit is often faster and \u000d\u000amore cost effective than an ED visit.\u000d\u000a\u2022 If they still decline, document refusal and which resources offered. ","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 110\u000d\u000aPlan of Care\u000d\u000aThe patient has no time to note or save the patient callback \u000d\u000anumber before getting into the rideshare\u000d\u000a\u2022 Provide the information before requesting the ride so the patient has \u000d\u000atime to take down the number and fully grasp the plan.\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Nurse can also schedule the ride to give patient time to get \u000d\u000aready (as NMTARA level allows) \u000d\u000a\u2022 If sending a patient to virtual care, go over the plan with them before \u000d\u000aconferencing in the care coordinator. Provide the callback number and \u000d\u000aadvise them of a follow-up survey via next business day phone call. ","Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 111\u000d\u000aAnswer\u000d\u000aRefer to your NMTARA level guidelines. The timer resets after 4 min of no \u000d\u000aresponse, up to12 min max. Call for a BLS response if no response after 12 \u000d\u000amin. If pickup time is out of range, be sure to select this in Corti.\u000d\u000aAnswer\u000d\u000aIf a minor (younger than 18 years old) calls with no adult present, we will send \u000d\u000aback to EMS to dispatch an ambulance.\u000d\u000aAnswer\u000d\u000aEach Contract has a list of determinants that tells them which calls are eligible for \u000d\u000a911 Nurse Navigation. This list is not for us to screen which calls we accept and \u000d\u000aassess.\u000d\u000aQuestion\u000d\u000aHow do we process calls \u000d\u000afrom minors?\u000d\u000aQuestion\u000d\u000aWhat if Transport.net \u000d\u000adoesn\u2019t work for me?\u000d\u000aQuestion\u000d\u000aIs there a list of call \u000d\u000ascenarios / types we should \u000d\u000areceive?","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 112\u000d\u000aAnswer\u000d\u000aBased on the nurse\u2019s identification and evaluation of red flag symptoms and the \u000d\u000aclinical protocol\u2019s care suggestions\u000d\u000a\u2022 BLS Response: Non-Emergent Response \u000d\u000a\u27a2 At the normal speed of traffic \u000d\u000a\u27a2 Units could be diverted to an emergency call nearby\u000d\u000a\u2022 BLS Response Consideration:\u000d\u000a\u27a2 The patient requires services only a hospital can provide\u000d\u000a\u27a2 The patient is immobile (bed bound, unable to walk, etc\u2026)\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Recommended mode of transportation by a healthcare provider\u000d\u000a\u2022 ALS Response: Emergent Response\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Lights and sirens\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Full speed ahead (goes through red lights) \u000d\u000a\u27a2 Won\u2019t be diverted\u000d\u000a\u2022 ALS Response Consideration:\u000d\u000a\u27a2 The patient requires advanced medical care such as:\u000d\u000ao cardiac monitoring\u000d\u000ao intubation\u000d\u000ao medication administration\u000d\u000ao IV access\u000d\u000ao Life-threatening emergencies like:\u000d\u000ao respiratory distress\u000d\u000ao MI related chest pain\u000d\u000ao stroke-like symptoms\u000d\u000aQuestion\u000d\u000aHow do I decide between \u000d\u000aan ALS or BLS response?","Dispositions \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 113\u000d\u000aVirtual Care (VC) / Telehealth\u000d\u000aPartner: RelyMD\u000d\u000aNMTARA 0-5\u000d\u000a \u000d\u000a \u000d\u000aClinical Staff\u000d\u000aEmergency Department \u000d\u000aBoarded Physicians as \u000d\u000awell as other providers \u000d\u000alike PAs and NPs.\u000d\u000aAvailability \u000d\u000aAvailable per provider's \u000d\u000aself-schedule: \u201cUber\u201d-\u000d\u000astyle model\u000d\u000aCheck availability \u000d\u000abefore offering!\u000d\u000aPlatform\u000d\u000aPrefer smart-device,\u000d\u000abut not necessary to \u000d\u000aconnect on scene.\u000d\u000aInsurance\u000d\u000aNOT insurance \u000d\u000adependent\u000d\u000aAge\u000d\u000a>2 years old","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 114\u000d\u000aCoverage Check\u000d\u000a\u2022 Make sure you have a provider available in the state your patient is currently in.\u000d\u000a\u2022 ER means there's an ER doc available for all your NMTARA 0 needs.\u000d\u000a\u2022 UC means there's an urgent care provider on for all your NMTARA 1-5 patients.","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 115\u000d\u000aCoverage Requests\u000d\u000a\u2022 If you're missing a provider for your patient, you can click the Report button, to help track \u000d\u000athe specific gap in coverage.\u000d\u000a\u2022 You can also ask a care coordinator in the chat if a provider available in the state your \u000d\u000apatient is in. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Check this Info icon if you are on the fence about VC. You can get to this list by clicking \u000d\u000athe info icon to the right of coverage:\u000d\u000ai","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 116\u000d\u000aVirtual Care \u000d\u000aExclusion Criteria\u000d\u000aGeneral Exclusions\u000d\u000aAge Criteria Exceptions\u000d\u000a\u2022 All patients under two years old\u000d\u000a\u2022 Patients 17 or younger without parental / guardian consent\u000d\u000aMobility Exceptions\u000d\u000a\u2022 Patient is non-ambulatory (cannot walk) without available or reasonable assistance \u000d\u000afrom transportation\u000d\u000aMedication Management\u000d\u000a\u2022 Patients likely to required scheduled narcotics or controlled substance refills\u000d\u000aAdvanced Live Support (ALS) Management\u000d\u000a\u2022 Any condition clearly requiring immediate ALS intervention\u000d\u000aNeurological Symptom Exceptions\u000d\u000aSudden Onset or Severe Headache\u000d\u000a\u2022 Example: \u201cWorst headache of my life\u201d within the last four hours\u000d\u000aSudden Onset Sustained Weakness, Numbness, or Paralysis\u000d\u000a\u2022 Especially unilateral within the last 4 hours ","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 117\u000d\u000aVirtual Care \u000d\u000aPreparation & Contact\u000d\u000aOverview\u000d\u000aComplete Prescreen Confirm Virtual Care Contact Virtual Care\u000d\u000aTrack Consultation Followthrough\u000d\u000a1. Prescreen Questions\u000d\u000aBefore you enroll this patient for a virtual care visit, please review the following information:\u000d\u000a5. Is the patient a minor (< 18 y.o.):\u000d\u000a\u2022 RelyMD does not see patient < 2 years of age.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Patients age 2-17 need a parent / guardian present to consent for VC treatment.\u000d\u000a6. RelyMD does not prescribe scheduled medications.\u000d\u000a7. RelyMD is not an appropriate solution for patients with:\u000d\u000a\u2022 ALS symptoms\u000d\u000a\u2022 Active suicidal ideation or behaviors\u000d\u000a\u2022 Active homicidal ideation or behaviors\u000d\u000a\u2022 Active psychosis or severe agitation\u000d\u000a1 2 3\u000d\u000a4 5","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 118\u000d\u000a2. Virtual Care Teams Confirmation\u000d\u000aInform the patient to start their virtual visit, there will be an intake process very similar to\u000d\u000achecking in at the doctor or ER. Advise the pt that if there is a disconnect during transfer, they \u000d\u000ashould turn off spam blockers and expect a call from an 855 number to complete this intake.\u000d\u000aAt this time, inform the patient that you will follow up with them if they require further care and \u000d\u000aif not, they will receive a follow up call to\u000d\u000aThen, put the following in the NN / Care Coordinator chat:\u000d\u000aPt Name, DOB, Address, Active callback number, U.S. State pt is calling from.","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 119\u000d\u000a3. Initiate Virtual Care Contact\u000d\u000a1. Keep the patient on hold to start the transfer.\u000d\u000a2. Dial (855) 879-4332\u000d\u000a\u2022 Option 9, 1, 1.\u000d\u000a3. Once the Care Coordinator answers confirm the information sent in the chat and verbally\u000d\u000agive pt age, gender and situation.\u000d\u000a4. Bring patient on the line and confirm everyone is on the call before disconnecting.\u000d\u000aExample: Genesys Consult Transfer\u000d\u000a*When a consult transfer is initiated, the patient will be placed on Hold automatically.\u000d\u000a8558794332","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 120\u000d\u000a4. Track the Consultation\u000d\u000aMonitor the RelyMD chat for updates from the provider. In the event the provider does not send \u000d\u000aa message, be sure to check the chart and follow through to make sure you do not miss further \u000d\u000anecessary care.\u000d\u000a5. Follow-Through\u000d\u000a\u2022 If your patient has been seen by the RelyMD provider and they recommend in-person\u000d\u000aevaluation, follow the steps below:\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Copy the incident (with comments)\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Update the Response Plan / Status on the new incident\u000d\u000aSelection Purpose\u000d\u000aThe provider recommends they go to the ER via ambulance (ALS or BLS)\u000d\u000aThe provider recommends they go to an urgent care clinic\u000d\u000aThe provider recommends they go to the ER via rideshare","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 121\u000d\u000aJournal\u000d\u000a\u2022 Click the plus sign to add a note that includes the provider\u2019s recommendation and the \u000d\u000aaction taken by the nurse.\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Example: \u201cNurse Navigation assist to nearest ED via EMS\u201d. Patient notified of the \u000d\u000aprovider\u2019s recommendation that he/she go to the ER via ambulance. Dispatch \u000d\u000acalled for BLS.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Click the plus sign to update the disposition to the recommended care option.","Documentation Do\u2019s & Don\u2019ts \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 122\u000d\u000aDocumentation\u000d\u000a\u2022 Tells the story of the patient encounter\u000d\u000a\u2022 Provides follow up information\u000d\u000a\u2022 Demonstrates that we did good work\u000d\u000a\u2022 Stands as a legal record of patient care.\u000d\u000aSomeone reading your after-call note should understand \u000d\u000aclearly what happened during the call without having to listen \u000d\u000ato it for additional context. \u000d\u000aYour ACW Timer\u000d\u000aIf the After Call Work (ACW) timer runs out before you \u000d\u000afinish documenting and another call comes in:\u000d\u000a1. Let the Call Roll\u000d\u000a2. Put yourself into Extended After Call Work (EACW)\u000d\u000a3. Finish your documentation\u000d\u000a4. Going forward always note your ACW timer","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 123\u000d\u000aSBARF\u000d\u000aSituation\u000d\u000aBackground\u000d\u000aAssessment\u000d\u000aRecommendation\u000d\u000aFollow Through\u000d\u000aAll Deviations from Protocol MUST be Documented\u000d\u000aWhat is the current chief complaint?\u000d\u000aRelevant history\u000d\u000aInclude vitals and Corti summarization\u000d\u000aCare options offered / declined / accepted\u000d\u000aActions taken by nurse to facilitate care","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 124\u000d\u000aGuidelines\u000d\u000a\u274e DON\u2019Ts\u000d\u000a\u2022 Chart opinion-based notes. Only document facts. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Copy and paste the unedited Corti AI summary.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Submit journal without checking spelling /grammar\u000d\u000a\u2022 Document what isn't reflected in the Corti session\u000d\u000a\u2714 DOs\u000d\u000a\u2022 Accurate spelling of patient\u2019s full name and physical address\u000d\u000a\u2022 Appropriate capitalization and inclusion of apartment / building / unit numbers\u000d\u000a\u2022 Be concise and clear in your communication\u000d\u000a\u2022 Enter patient information in the appropriate fields\u000d\u000a\u2022 Verify who the caller (name) is and their relationship to the patient\u000d\u000a\u2022 The patient\u2019s phone number may be different from the caller\u2019s phone number. \u000d\u000a\u27a2 Do not enter the EMT / Medic\u2019s number here.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Call tags are NOT optional! You must select one of three:\u000d\u000a\u27a2 911 call taker\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Field Fire\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Field AMR","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 125\u000d\u000aDocumentation Layout\u000d\u000aAfter you open your CAD-to-CAD call on the right side, click the Being Evaluated button so that\u000d\u000ayour team will know you are working on the call. \u000d\u000aA B\u000d\u000aC D\u000d\u000aE\u000d\u000aF\u000d\u000aG\u000d\u000aH","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 126\u000d\u000aOverview\u000d\u000aA. Click for Patient Info Screen.\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Enter the patient\u2019s information and ensure all required fields are completed.\u000d\u000aB. Enter Contract Name.\u000d\u000aC. Enter the caller\u2019s name and relationship to the patient. \u000d\u000aD. Enter the caller\u2019s phone number.\u000d\u000a\u27a2 The caller\u2019s phone number may be different from the patient\u2019s phone number. \u000d\u000a\u27a2 Do not enter the EMT / Medic\u2019s number in this section.\u000d\u000aE. Enter the patient\u2019s address details.\u000d\u000aF. Select insurance type.\u000d\u000aG. Input the Reference / Event Number.\u000d\u000aH. Call tags are NOT optional! You must select one of three:\u000d\u000a\u27a2 911 call taker\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Field Fire\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Field AMR","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 127\u000d\u000aPatient Overview Window\u000d\u000aRequired entry fields are:\u000d\u000a\u2022 First Name\u000d\u000a\u2022 Last Name\u000d\u000a\u2022 Phone Number (use dashes)\u000d\u000a\u2022 Date of Birth\u000d\u000a\u2022 Gender\u000d\u000a\u2022 Address\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Include apt. / building / unit number","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 128\u000d\u000aI. Select the contract type from the Response Plan / Status menu on the right. \u000d\u000aJ. For a clinic referral, select REF from the Response Plan / Status menu. \u000d\u000aK. From the list of clinics, select the one with the closest time. \u000d\u000aL. If the name and address of the desired clinic are not listed in the Queue Times window, \u000d\u000aenter them manually into the Delivery field. \u000d\u000aPatient, Ima\u000d\u000a911 NC \u2013 Wake County\u000d\u000aCaller\u2019s Name 555-555-5555\u000d\u000a475 Quiet Hill Road, Hollycrest NC, 27013\u000d\u000aDoor Code 4879\u000d\u000a[Call Taker] Call Taker\u000d\u000aI\u000d\u000aJ\u000d\u000aK\u000d\u000aL\u000d\u000aTo","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 129\u000d\u000aEditing the Corti Summary\u000d\u000a \u000d\u000a \u000d\u000a \u000d\u000a \u000d\u000a \u000d\u000aPatient Age Patient Sex Chief Complaint\u000d\u000aReported \u000d\u000aSymptoms\u000d\u000aRelevant Past \u000d\u000aMedical History\u000d\u000aCurrent \u000d\u000aMedications\u000d\u000aNMTARA\u000d\u000aLevel\u000d\u000aRecommended \u000d\u000aDisposition\u000d\u000aPatient\u2019s \u000d\u000aAcceptance of Plan\u000d\u000aEducation Provided \u000d\u000ato Patient\u000d\u000aCorti Session ID\u000d\u000aDate / Time \u000d\u000aInformation","Follow-Up\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 130\u000d\u000aCircle back to document patient outcomes, if known.\u000d\u000aAdd a note, DO NOT edit an existing note.\u000d\u000a\u2713 Ride Completed\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Ride home requested / completed\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Virtual Care follow up \u000d\u000a\u27a2 TIP, VC > REF, VC > EMS\u000d\u000a\u2713 Clinical Disposition\u000d\u000a\u27a2 What is the consultation outcome?\u000d\u000a\u2713 Do NOT include the provider\u2019s name in the note\u000d\u000a\u2713 Did patient need a ride to a different clinic?\u000d\u000aRide completion should be \u000d\u000adocumented in a timely \u000d\u000amanner to confirm completion \u000d\u000aof transportation and ensure \u000d\u000athe patient requires no further \u000d\u000acare from us.","Quality Assurance \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 131\u000d\u000aGuiding Scope & Principles\u000d\u000a\u2022 Observers of 911 NN\u2019s efforts to ensure safe and appropriate patient care\u000d\u000a\u2022 Use objective metrics based on stated standards and processes\u000d\u000a\u2022 Every call reviewed is an opportunity to reinforce what we\u2019re doing well, move us closer \u000d\u000ato a unified patient experience, and identify areas for NN improvement\u000d\u000aWhat We Do\u000d\u000aRoutine Evaluations Each nurse is scored twice per month\u000d\u000aCall Investigations Both Internal & External\u000d\u000aSpecial Assignments Analysis of call types for better understanding, workflow \u000d\u000aimprovement, and systems checks. \u000d\u000aReporting Research and report trends and findings to the proper \u000d\u000astakeholder(s)\u000d\u000aReporting\u000d\u000a\u2022 Calls within normal expectations will be discussed at scheduled 1:1s\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Goal: same-day visibility on NN \u201creport card\u201d\u000d\u000a\u2022 Flagged calls allow for timely guidance supporting continual improvement\u000d\u000a\u27a2 If you report to a Supervisor, reports go to Supervisor and Manager\u000d\u000a\u27a2 If you report to a Manager, reports go to Manager and Director\u000d\u000aQA Rubric Goals & Development\u000d\u000aDeveloped from the \u000d\u000aConversation Guide\u000d\u000aDesigned to minimize \u000d\u000asubjectivity and eliminate bias \u000d\u000aEvaluates adherence \u000d\u000ato workflows\u000d\u000aCall Handling & Documentation \u000d\u000aare both graded","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 132\u000d\u000aCall Handling\u000d\u000aRaise your Hand \u2013 3 pts\u000d\u000a\u2610 The nurse used the appropriate greeting for the call. (3 pts)\u000d\u000aKeep Care at the Center \u2013 35 pts\u000d\u000a\u2610 The nurse informed the patient/caller they were on a recorded line. (5 pts)\u000d\u000a\u2610 The nurse appropriately verbalized that there was no ambulance on the way / why the \u000d\u000acall was routed to a nurse. (5 pts)\u000d\u000a\u2610 The nurse verified HIPP data of the patient (name, date, and phone). (10 pts)\u000d\u000a\u2610 The nurse verified insurance with the patient/caller. (5 pts)\u000d\u000a\u2610 The nurse verified the incident address and disconnect phone number with the \u000d\u000apatient/caller. (10 pts)\u000d\u000aSeek to Understand \u2013 28 pts\u000d\u000a\u2610 The nurse spoke with the patient / asked to speak with the patient. (8 pts)\u000d\u000a\u2610 The nurse probed chief complaint and red flag symptoms. (10 pts)\u000d\u000a\u2610 The nurse chose and accurately followed an appropriate triage pathway. (10 pts)\u000d\u000aFind a Way Together \u2013 24 pts\u000d\u000a\u2610 Care resources were presented one at a time. (3 pts)\u000d\u000a\u2610 Care recommendations were appropriate given NMTARA and known barriers. (8 pts)\u000d\u000a\u2610 Plan of Care was outlined with the patient. (8 pts) \u000d\u000a\u2022 Where they\u2019re getting seen \u000d\u000a\u2022 How they\u2019re getting there \u000d\u000a\u2022 What to take with \u000d\u000a\u2022 Who to call for next steps or breaks in the plan\u000d\u000a\u2610 The patient agreed/verbalized understanding of the PoC. (5 pts)\u000d\u000aBe Accountable \u2013 10 pts\u000d\u000a\u2610 Care arrangements initiated per disposition specifications (10 pts) \u000d\u000a\u2022 Ambulance \u2013 responsible party was informed per contract instructions \u000d\u000a\u2022 Private transport \u2013 destination selected in software and transport finalized \u000d\u000a\u2022 Telephonic \u2013 followed instructions to successful warm handoff \u000d\u000aKudos: Did the nurse do something exceptionally well, or go above and beyond on this call?","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 133\u000d\u000aDocumentation \u000d\u000aCustomer Field \u2013 16 pts\u000d\u000a\u2610 Caller (911 Contract) (6 pts)\u000d\u000a\u2610 Phone (Disconnect callback number) (6 pts)\u000d\u000a\u2610 Applicant (Disconnect phone owner, with relationship if not patient) (4 pts)\u000d\u000aPatient Info Field \u2013 24 pts\u000d\u000a\u2610 First and Last Name (spelling verified) (8 pts)\u000d\u000a\u2610 Phone (verified as pt\u2019s) (6 pts)\u000d\u000a\u2610 DOB (8 pts)\u000d\u000a\u2610 Gender (2 pts)\u000d\u000aFrom Field \u2013 9 pts\u000d\u000a\u2610 Address (8 pts)\u000d\u000a\u2610 Additional Data (if needed) (1 pts)\u000d\u000aBooking Field \u2013 9 pts\u000d\u000a\u2610 Cause (triage pathway) (6 pts)\u000d\u000a\u2610 Tags (source of call) (2 pts)\u000d\u000a\u2610 Referral (if given) (1 pts)\u000d\u000aResponse Plan Field \u2013 16 pts\u000d\u000a\u2610 Contract (insurance) (4 pts)\u000d\u000a\u2610 Disposition (8 pts)\u000d\u000a\u2610 Resource selected (if applicable) (4 pts)\u000d\u000aJournal Screen \u2013 28 pts\u000d\u000a\u2610 Note: SBARF used \u2013 4 pts\u000d\u000a\u2610 Note: Deviations (NMTARA or process) documented \u2013 6 pts\u000d\u000a\u2610 Note: Narrative details match call \u2013 8 pts\u000d\u000a\u2610 Note: Corti ID documented \u2013 6 pts\u000d\u000a\u2610 NMTARA: correct for call \u2013 4 pts","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 134\u000d\u000aFlags\u000d\u000a_________________\u000d\u000aCustomer Service Issue\u000d\u000a\u2022 Unprofessional conduct (lack of empathy, frequent interruptions, rude, dismissive, etc.)\u000d\u000a\u2022 Negative statements re: pt eligibility/qualifications for EMS or pt situation\u000d\u000a\u2022 Nurse statements disparaged EMS system or capabilities\u000d\u000a\u2022 Nurse\u2019s actions were not in alignment with contract-specific guidance\u000d\u000a\u2022 ALS escalation reasoning unclear\u000d\u000a\u2022 NMTARA 6 / Triage Not Complete reasoning unclear\u000d\u000aPatient Safety Issue\u000d\u000a\u2022 Red flag symptoms\u000d\u000a\u2022 Did not utilize triage pathway or used inappropriate triage pathway\u000d\u000a\u2022 Care recommendation lower than NMTARA classification\u000d\u000a\u2022 Exclusion criteria met, continued triage","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 135\u000d\u000aKeys to Success\u000d\u000aFollow the Conversation Guide\u000d\u000aIt was designed to keep all of 911 NN on track!\u000d\u000aUse the Tools that are There to Help You \u000d\u000aCorti, Genesys tags, whisper, etc.\u000d\u000aVerify HIPAA Data\u000d\u000aThe importance of this only grows as we evolve our work with clients and payers.\u000d\u000aDocument Clinical Reasoning for Deviations\u000d\u000aTriage Not Completed - NMTARA 6 / Exclusion Criteria\u000d\u000aCare escalation above NMTARA expectations\u000d\u000aAsk for Help When You Need It\u000d\u000aWe are here to help you! ","Transportation Guide \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 136\u000d\u000aTransport.Net\u000d\u000aGMR\u2019s web-based solution for ride ordering\u000d\u000aThe plan is to utilize \ud83d\udd17Transport.net for ride ordering on all contracts over time. \u000d\u000a\u2022 1\u000d\u000ast Contract: 911 CA, Santa Clara \u000d\u000a\u2022 2\u000d\u000and Contract: 911 WA, King County (GoLive 12.10.24) \u000d\u000aRight now, NN is only using Transport.Net for BLS ambulance requests \u000d\u000a\u2022 Future state: \u000d\u000a\u27a2 Rideshare Requests will shop Lyft and Uber for the lowest fare \u000d\u000a\u27a2 One-click ordering from within Logis\u000d\u000aNo, we don\u2019t have an ETA","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 137\u000d\u000aWorkflow\u000d\u000aCORTI will guide you in what to do.\u000d\u000aSign in via Okta chiclet\u000d\u000aFill in the info into the correct fields\u000d\u000aChoose the \u000d\u000aContract/Facility\u000d\u000aAddress & Comments\u000d\u000aNMTARA\u000d\u000aDemographics\u000d\u000aClick \u201c+ New Request\u201d\u000d\u000aClick \u201cSend\u201d","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 138\u000d\u000aTransport.Net Form\u000d\u000aSend Save Draft Cancel","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 139\u000d\u000aWhat\u2019s Next?\u000d\u000a\u2022 Wait for a response: can take up to 8 minutes\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Sends request to vendors and allows 4 minutes for reply. \u000d\u000a\u27a2 If no response, sends again.\u000d\u000a\u27a2 If still no response, you will get message that no vendors are available. \u000d\u000a\u2022 If accepted: check against contract\u2019s guidelines in Corti. \u000d\u000a\u27a2 If within guidelines, choose \u201cBLS Transport arranged within guidelines\u201d and \u000d\u000afollow Corti instructions.\u000d\u000a\u27a2 If outside guidelines, choose \u201cBLS Transport\u2019s ETA outside NMTARA guidelines,\u201d\u000d\u000afollow instructions. \u000d\u000a\u2022 If not accepted: choose \u201cBLS Transport not picked up by provider\u201d and follow Corti \u000d\u000ainstructions\u000d\u000aLimitations\u000d\u000a\u2022 Needs a numbered address \u000d\u000a\u27a2 If your patient is at a street corner, ask what building they\u2019re in front of and look \u000d\u000ait up on Google Maps. \u000d\u000a\u27a2 If your patient is on the side of the highway, use the backup option (this will vary \u000d\u000aby contract). \u000d\u000a\u2022 Can take up to 8 minutes to get a final result \u000d\u000a\u27a2 Sends request to vendors and allows 4 minutes to reply. \u000d\u000a\u27a2 If no response, send again. \u000d\u000a\u27a2 If still no response, will then notify that no vendors are available.","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 140\u000d\u000aLyft: Preferred Transportation in most contracts\u000d\u000aLog in at the beginning of your shift and leave open for the shift.","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 141\u000d\u000a1. You must enter the patient's first and last name, telephone number (does not need to be \u000d\u000acell but it is preferred). Pick up address and drop off address should be entered manually \u000d\u000ainstead of copy and paste.\u000d\u000a2. Note for the driver: information that is important or helpful to the driver. \"Rider is \u000d\u000aelderly and may take a few minutes.\" Or \"Rider wearing a yellow hat.\"\u000d\u000a3. Select standard ride or wait and save if the patient needs more time to get ready.","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 142\u000d\u000a4. Enter request notes (Internal note):\u000d\u000a\u27a2 You must enter the contract and destination.\u000d\u000ao Ex: Seattle-ER, Knox-Pharmacy, Wake-Urgent Care, etc\u000d\u000a5. Select Request Ride for driver information","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 143\u000d\u000aDriver Details\u000d\u000a\u2022 Patients usually receive a text with driver info but if they have not, provide name and car \u000d\u000ainfo with ETA.\u000d\u000a\u2022 You MUST document the Ride ID in your journal as well as confirmation that your patient \u000d\u000ahas reached their destination.","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 144\u000d\u000aThe Uber Alternative \u000d\u000aSame process, different platform.","Workflows 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 145\u000d\u000a1. Confirm the rider arrived at their destination \u000d\u000a2. Document\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Document Trip ID to the journal.\u000d\u000ao Example: Abc12345-abc1234-abc123456-abc123","Page 146\u000d\u000aSystem Applications\u000d\u000aIn This Section\u000d\u000aCan\u2019t remember how to do a warm handoff in Genesys? Need a \u000d\u000arefresher on how to edit your signature? Systems and Applications is \u000d\u000ayour stop for all programs and platforms that make your job easier.","Reference Topics \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 147\u000d\u000aWorkstation Setup\u000d\u000aUltimate Kronos Group (UKG)\u000d\u000aGenesys\u000d\u000aCAD-to-CAD\u000d\u000aLogis\u000d\u000aCrisp DC\u000d\u000aDC Taxi","Workstation Setup\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 148\u000d\u000aIntroduction\u000d\u000aThis section will explain how to access and set up vital applications such as Teams, Okta, and \u000d\u000aOutlook. Learn how to customize your Outlook signature, Teams notifications, and bookmarks. \u000d\u000aLogging In\u000d\u000a\u2022 Log onto the workstation with your username (email address) and temporary password\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Your email address is usually: firstname.lastname@gmr.net\u000d\u000a\u2022 Your temporary password is your:\u000d\u000a\u27a2 [Birthmonth][Last 5 of SSN]! \u000d\u000a\u27a2 (no spaces; capitalize firstletter of month)\u000d\u000a\u2022 You will be prompted to create a new password and set up forgotten password questions\u000d\u000aApplications Access\u000d\u000aOkta Teams Outlook\u000d\u000aDigital applications hub used \u000d\u000ato access Teams, Outlook, \u000d\u000aCornerstone, Transport.net, \u000d\u000aand more!\u000d\u000aUsed to communicate with \u000d\u000ayour trainer, supervisor, and \u000d\u000ateam. Also use to access NNspecific resources.\u000d\u000aReview emails regarding \u000d\u000aorganization updates and \u000d\u000aannouncements. ","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 149\u000d\u000aOkta\u000d\u000aTo access Okta, open Microsoft Edge and navigate to: \ud83d\udd17 https://gmr.okta.com/\u000d\u000a\u2022 Enter your GMR username, password, and use Google Authenticator to login\u000d\u000aUse Okta as to quickly find and open job-essential web applications:\u000d\u000aCan\u2019t find the app you\u2019re looking for? Use the search bar at the top of the page:","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 150\u000d\u000aWhen new apps are added to your Okta dashboard, you will receive a notification on the leftside navigation menu: \u000d\u000aWhy Use Okta?\u000d\u000aOkta ensures a safe, secure, and seamless \u000d\u000anavigation experience when you switch \u000d\u000abetween applications. ","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 151\u000d\u000aTeams\u000d\u000aAccess Teams from Okta (and bookmark for future use)\u000d\u000a\u2022 Teams can filter your communications into Unread, Channels, and Chats\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Select the Unread filter to display any unread message you have received in a \u000d\u000achat or channel\u000d\u000a\u27a2 You will be added to organization-specific channels, such as NN Academy, to help \u000d\u000ayou access resources necessary to do your job\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Select Chats to view individual or team chats that are not affiliated with an \u000d\u000aorganization-specific channel\u000d\u000aImport Favorites from Teams\u000d\u000aWe have consolidated the most-used web pages and applications into a list of Favorites \u000d\u000a(bookmarked websites) that you can import into Microsoft Edge:\u000d\u000a1. Open the NN Academy > General Teams channel\u000d\u000a2. Select the \u201cFiles\u201d tab at the top of the channel window\u000d\u000aFolder Navigation\u000d\u000a\ud83d\udcc1Day 1 > \ud83d\udcc1Policies > \ud83d\udcc1Workstation Setup ","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 152\u000d\u000a3. Right click or select the three dots beside the file\u2019s name to download the\u000d\u000a\ud83d\uddce bookmarks 7_25-25 file\u000d\u000a4. On the Edge browser, click the three dots near the upper right corner to access settings\u000d\u000a5. Click favorites to access the list\u000d\u000a\u2026","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 153\u000d\u000a6. Click the three dots next to the pin and select import favorites","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 154\u000d\u000a7. Under Select import browser data now click \u201cChoose what to import\u201d\u000d\u000a8. From the drop down, select Favorites or bookmarks html file\u000d\u000a9. Select the bookmarks_7_25_25 file from your computer\u2019s Downloads folder\u000d\u000a10. In your address bar, enter edge://favorites/ and toggle show favorites bar to \u201calways\u201d","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 155\u000d\u000aSetting your Signature in Outlook\u000d\u000a1. Open Outlook from your web browser\u000d\u000a2. Under File, select Settings\u000d\u000a3. Under Account > Signature, select \u201cAdd Signature\u201d","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 156\u000d\u000a4. Name your signature\u000d\u000ao Example: \u201cDefault\u201d\u000d\u000a5. Copy / Paste the email signature located in the NN Academy Teams folder:\u000d\u000aFolder Navigation\u000d\u000a\ud83d\udcc1Day 1 > \ud83d\udcc1Policies > \ud83d\udcc1Workstation Setup \u000d\u000a6. Once pasted into Outlook, edit the signature to match your information\u000d\u000ao Your name and credentials\u000d\u000ao Nurse Navigator, 911 Nurse Navigation\u000d\u000ao Phone number\u000d\u000a\u25aa Lewisville: 972-204-5092\u000d\u000a\u25aa Phoenix: 623-201-6069\u000d\u000a7. Check \u201cSet default for new messages\u201d\u000d\u000a8. Save","Ultimate Kronos Group (UKG)\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 157\u000d\u000aIntroduction\u000d\u000aUltimate Kronos Group: This application is nurses clock in and out, check the schedule, and \u000d\u000aenter PTO requests. You can also clock in and out using the time clock on the wall near the \u000d\u000aprinter. \u000d\u000aAgents can use UKG to:\u000d\u000aClock in and Out\u000d\u000aRequest Time Off\u000d\u000aReview Attendance Records\u000d\u000aUKG helps managers balance staffing levels with expected call demand by:\u000d\u000a \u000d\u000a \u000d\u000aFor additional reference, there are videos available in Cornerstone. While these videos provide a \u000d\u000ageneral overview of UKG and how request PTO / Shift swaps, please note that what we \u000d\u000adiscussed was specifically related to 911 Nurse Navigation.\u000d\u000aTroubleshooting Schedule Alterations\u000d\u000aFor UKG-related issues:\u000d\u000aSydney.Jaramillo@gmr.net\u000d\u000aScheduling issue, PTO / Shift \u000d\u000aswap / Overtime request:\u000d\u000aNathan.Herron@gmr.net\u000d\u000a1\u000d\u000a2\u000d\u000a3\u000d\u000aForecasting \u000d\u000aWorkforce Needs \u000d\u000aIdentifying \u000d\u000aStaffing Gaps\u000d\u000aManaging Overtime\u000d\u000aSupporting shift \u000d\u000aswaps and schedule \u000d\u000aadjustments","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 158\u000d\u000aClocking In and Out\u000d\u000aClick Punch In to clock in for your shift. Click Punch Out at the end of your shift. We do not clock \u000d\u000ain or out for lunch. \u000d\u000aMissing Punches\u000d\u000aThe Fix Missing Punches button is used if you forget to clock in or out. It allows you to enter the \u000d\u000amissing time to ensure your hours are correct. \u000d\u000a\u2022 If you arrive on time but experience delays clocking in, do not punch in late. Instead, use \u000d\u000athe 'Fix Missing Punches' option at the end of your shift.\u000d\u000a\u2022 When using Fix Missing Punches, enter the date and time for the missed punch, then \u000d\u000asave your entry. \u000d\u000a\u27a2 After submission, Sydney will review and approve the missing punch request \u000d\u000aaccordingly. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Please allow Sydney time to review and approve your missing punch request. \u000d\u000aAvoid Duplications\u000d\u000aThere's no need to submit it more than once. Submitting multiple requests can result in \u000d\u000aduplicates, which may lead to one being approved and the other denied after her reviews. To \u000d\u000aavoid confusion, it's best to submit your request only once and allow time for processing. \u000d\u000aYou cannot clock in any earlier \u000d\u000athan 10 minutes before your \u000d\u000ashift start time without \u000d\u000amanagement approval.","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 159\u000d\u000aMy Time Card\u000d\u000a\u2022 You are expected to check your timecard at the beginning and end of your shift. \u000d\u000a\u2022 If you encounter issues submitting the correction, take a screenshot (using the Snipping \u000d\u000aTool) and email the issue to Sydney the image along with a completed Time Exception \u000d\u000aForm so Payroll can address the issue. \u000d\u000a\u2022 You can check your PTO balance by selecting the Accruals option at the bottom of the \u000d\u000apage in this tile.","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 160\u000d\u000aTelestaff Roster Tile\u000d\u000aThis tile displays who is scheduled and their start and end times.\u000d\u000aTelestaff Roster codes you will see: \u000d\u000a \u000d\u000a\u201cRD\u201d Regular Duty\u000d\u000aA Standard Shift\u000d\u000aRXSOT40Sa\u000d\u000aAn Overtime Shift\u000d\u000aSTW\u000d\u000aShift Trade Working \u000d\u000a(Shift swaps)","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 161\u000d\u000aRequesting Time Off or Shift Swap\u000d\u000a\u2022 On the View My Schedule tile, select view my schedule. \u000d\u000a\u2022 This tile shows your current and upcoming shifts. \u000d\u000a\u2022 You can also submit PTO and shift swap requests here. \u000d\u000a\u27a2 Please follow the PTO Policy for all PTO and shift swap requests.","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 162\u000d\u000aPTO / Shift Swap\u000d\u000a\u2022 Click on the day you want to request. Select Add. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Choose if it is PTO or Shift Swap request. \u000d\u000a\u2022 The box will expand to include more areas to complete.","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 163\u000d\u000aYou are not allowed to request OT or shift swaps during the \u000d\u000atraining, and you must wait until week 10.","Genesys\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 164\u000d\u000aIntroduction\u000d\u000aGenesys is our phone and communication system used to manage inbound and outbound calls, \u000d\u000acustomer interactions, and team collaboration. \u000d\u000aThe platform:\u000d\u000aHelps ensure calls are routed to the right team members\u000d\u000aProvides access to call history and reporting\u000d\u000aSupports a seamless customer service experience\u000d\u000aGenesys call routing ensures customers are connected to the right person as efficiently as \u000d\u000apossible. The system uses information gathered from the caller, business rules, agent skills, and \u000d\u000areal-time availability to determine the best destination for each call, helping improve both \u000d\u000acustomer experience and operational efficiency.\u000d\u000a1\u000d\u000a2\u000d\u000a3\u000d\u000aTo learn more about how we are able to help our patients once their call is received, \u000d\u000aplease see the Workflows section of this document.","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 165\u000d\u000aQuick Links\u000d\u000aSelect a topic to view that section of the Genesys tutorial:\u000d\u000aIntroduction\u000d\u000a\u2022 Definitions\u000d\u000a\u2022 Sign Into Genesys\u000d\u000a\u2022 Cloud Components\u000d\u000a\u2022 Set Notification Preferences\u000d\u000a\u2022 Sound Preferences\u000d\u000a\u2022 Public Profile Overview\u000d\u000a\u2022 Log Out of Genesys\u000d\u000aInteractions\u000d\u000a\u2022 Non-ACD (Internal) Calls\u000d\u000a\u2022 ACD Interactions on Behalf of Queue\u000d\u000a\u2022 Call Dashboard\u000d\u000a\u2022 Call Consults & Conferences\u000d\u000aYour Status & Activities\u000d\u000a\u2022 Check Your Status\u000d\u000a\u2022 After Call Work (ACW) & Wrap-Up Codes\u000d\u000a\u2022 Failing to Answer an Interaction\u000d\u000a\u2022 View Performance & Queue Activity\u000d\u000aTroubleshooting\u000d\u000a\u2022 Common Errors","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 166\u000d\u000aDefinitions\u000d\u000aGenesys Cloud\u000d\u000aAn interaction management application that supports managing interactions including voice \u000d\u000acalls, voicemail, conference calls, chat, video calls, and email; media types may vary by \u000d\u000aorganization, department, and / or queue.\u000d\u000aWebRTC Phone\u000d\u000aWebRTC Phone runs directly from the internet browser with no special hardware \u000d\u000arequirements or additional software; a user\u2019s computer acts as their phone.\u000d\u000aQueue\u000d\u000aA \u201cwaiting line\u201d of interactions ready to be answered.\u000d\u000aNon-ACD Call Menu\u000d\u000aThe menu and associated calls that are on behalf of a queue.\u000d\u000aInteraction\u000d\u000aCommunications (calls) routed through the Queue to eligible nurses. \u000d\u000aInbound Call\u000d\u000aCalls arriving to 911 Nurse Navigation.\u000d\u000aOutbound Call\u000d\u000aCalls made from NN to an internal or external contact.\u000d\u000aConsult\u000d\u000aDuring a call, this is an option in Genesys that allows a contact to be placed on hold while a \u000d\u000asecondary contact is reached. It is possible to warm-transfer a caller with this feature. ","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 167\u000d\u000aConference\u000d\u000aDuring a call, this is an option in Genesys that allows all parties to speak to, and hear, one \u000d\u000aanother in real time. It is possible to transfer a contact using this feature. \u000d\u000aWrap-up Code / After Call Work (ACW)\u000d\u000aRequired ACW that appears after a call has ended on behalf of a queue.\u000d\u000aAgent Workspace\u000d\u000aThe main working component of Genesys Cloud where external inbound and outbound \u000d\u000ainteractions are managed. \u000d\u000aCold Transfer\u000d\u000aCold transfers will forward the caller to another contact without introduction or confirming \u000d\u000atheir ability to take the call.\u000d\u000aWarm Transfer\u000d\u000aOutreach is made to another contact before the caller is transferred. This allows us to \u000d\u000aprovide caller details, confirm the contacts availability to take the call, and summarize the \u000d\u000acaller\u2019s concerns. ","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 168\u000d\u000aSign Into Genesys\u000d\u000a1. Login to Okta: \u000d\u000a\ud83d\udd17 https://gmr.okta.com/\u000d\u000a2. Click on the Genesys chicklet.\u000d\u000aPlease use Google \u000d\u000aChrome when accessing \u000d\u000aGenesys Cloud.","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 169\u000d\u000a3. When prompted, click Collaborate / Communicate.\u000d\u000a4. A successful login will direct you to this screen: ","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 170\u000d\u000aCloud Components\u000d\u000aComponents / Icons may vary depending on screen resolution, browser window size, or browser \u000d\u000azoom level:\u000d\u000aYour PROFILE ICON (located in the upper-right \u000d\u000acorner of the Genesys window) is ESSENTIAL for\u000d\u000asetting your preferences, status management, and \u000d\u000alogging out of Genesys. ","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 171\u000d\u000aSet Notification Preferences \u000d\u000a5. Click Profile.\u000d\u000a6. Click Preferences.\u000d\u000a7. Ensure Notifications is selected from the left.\u000d\u000a8. Check the box for Allow Pop-up Notifications.\u000d\u000a9. Users may also need to enable pop-ups in their browser.","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 172\u000d\u000aSound Preferences\u000d\u000aBy default, Genesys will match the Sound Settings on your system. \u000d\u000a1. From the Preferences window, click Sound.\u000d\u000a2. Review the Audio Device Profile at the top.\u000d\u000a3. The profile listed in the dropdown is being used for calls, speakers, and microphones.","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 173\u000d\u000aTo create a new Sound Profile:\u000d\u000a1. Select New Profile from the Audio Device Profile dropdown. \u000d\u000a2. Name the Profile something recognizable:\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Follow the steps in the \ud83d\udd17Review Sound Preferences document\u000d\u000a3. Set Microphone, Speaker, and Alert selections. \u000d\u000a4. Click Save.","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 174\u000d\u000aPublic Profile Overview\u000d\u000aInformation about a user that is visible to all the organization\u2019s Genesys Cloud Users\u000d\u000aTo access:\u000d\u000a1. Click Profile.\u000d\u000a2. Click large profile icon or circle.\u000d\u000aHere, you can review your public profile as seen by others in the organization:","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 175\u000d\u000aA\u000d\u000aB\u000d\u000aC\u000d\u000aD\u000d\u000aA. Change Profile Picture\u000d\u000aB. Status\u000d\u000aC. Your Name\u000d\u000aD. Status Note","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 176\u000d\u000aLog Out of Genesys\u000d\u000a \u000d\u000aWait for the browser to fully sign you out of Genesys before closing it.\u000d\u000a1\u000d\u000aGo Off Queue\u000d\u000a2\u000d\u000aOpen your \u000d\u000aProfile Menu\u000d\u000a3\u000d\u000aClick Logout\u000d\u000a4\u000d\u000aClose your \u000d\u000atab / browser","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 177\u000d\u000aNon-ACD (Internal) Calls\u000d\u000aOutbound Non-ACD Calls\u000d\u000aUse the Calls component to make non-ACD internal and \u000d\u000aoutbound calls:\u000d\u000a\u2022 These are calls NOT on behalf of a queue.\u000d\u000aOutbound Non-ACD Calls\u000d\u000a1. Click the Calls icon.\u000d\u000a2. Click the + button from the top of the panel.\u000d\u000a3. Alternatively, you can click\u000d\u000a \u000d\u000ato enter a number or contact.\u000d\u000aYou will still be eligible to \u000d\u000areceive calls if you make \u000d\u000anon-ACD calls or calls NOT\u000d\u000aOn Behalf of a Queue.\u000d\u000a1\u000d\u000a2 3","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 178\u000d\u000aTo dial a Genesys Cloud User\u2026\u000d\u000a1. Type their name into the Number or Contact field at the top.\u000d\u000a2. Select it from the dropdown.\u000d\u000aTo dial externally\u2026\u000d\u000a1. Use the dial pad or your keyboard to type in a full, 10-digit number\u000d\u000a2. Press Enter on the keyboard.\u000d\u000a3 Click Enter on the keyboard OR the Green Phone Button (turns green when you enter \u000d\u000anumbers or letters)\u000d\u000aPhone Number / \u000d\u000aContact Entry\u000d\u000aStart \u000d\u000aCall","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 179\u000d\u000aInbound Non-ACD Calls\u000d\u000aWhen someone within the business attempts to contact you through Genesys, you will receive a \u000d\u000anotification in the upper right corner of your window:\u000d\u000a\u2022 Click Answer to take the call\u000d\u000a\u2022 Click the green Agent Workspace component to view interaction details (caller ID)\u000d\u000aIf already in the agent workspace, click Answer to take the call: ","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 180\u000d\u000aMute / Unmute\u000d\u000aHold\u000d\u000aTouch-Tone Dialpad \u000d\u000aMore Options\u000d\u000a\u2022 Record\u000d\u000a\u2022 Add Participant\u000d\u000a\u2022 Transfer\u000d\u000a\u2022 Voice Quality Issue\u000d\u000aEnd Call","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 181\u000d\u000aACD Interactions On Behalf of Queue\u000d\u000aOutbound Calls\u000d\u000aALL external calls MUST be made On Behalf of Queue\u000d\u000a\u2022 Interaction recording policy is applied.\u000d\u000a\u2022 If dialing while On-Queue, agent is not eligible for inbound interactions.\u000d\u000a\u2022 The caller ID number (determined by the On Behalf of Queue Field) routes the customer\u000d\u000a/ patient back to the queue rather than the individual agent.\u000d\u000aTo make an outbound call on behalf of a queue:\u000d\u000a1. From the Agent Workspace component, click the Start Conversation (phone) button. \u000d\u000a2. Search and select an outbound queue (the phone number we are calling from).\u000d\u000a3. Enter the phone number you wish to call\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Genesys will attempt to search its address book as you type the phone number. \u000d\u000aTo dismiss the address book, press enter on your keyboard after the phone \u000d\u000anumber after completing your entry. \u000d\u000a4. The Start Call button will turn green when both On Behalf of Queue and Phone Number\u000d\u000afields are completed. Press Enter on your keyboard or select this button to make a call. \u000d\u000a1. Start Conversation\u000d\u000a2. On Behalf of Queue\u000d\u000a3. Phone Number Field\u000d\u000a4. Start Call","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 182\u000d\u000aInbound Calls\u000d\u000aIncoming interactions are accompanied by a ring as well as two types of response methods:\u000d\u000aMethod 1: While in the Agent Workspace, select the blue Answer button when the \u000d\u000ainteraction notification appears on the left-side of the screen. \u000d\u000a\u2022 This notification will indicate the queue through which the interaction \u000d\u000awas routed. \u000d\u000aMethod 2: Anywhere in Genesys, you will see a smaller notification appear in the upperright corner of the window (below your profile icon). \u000d\u000a\u2022 Click Answer to accept the interaction.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Click View to open the Agent Workspace component. \u000d\u000aMethod 1\u000d\u000aMethod 2","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 183\u000d\u000aA\u000d\u000aDisplays the general location the call is coming from:\u000d\u000a\u2022 In this example, the call is coming from Frisco, TX\u000d\u000aB This is the call\u2019s timer\u000d\u000aC Interaction Type\u000d\u000aD The caller\u2019s phone number\u000d\u000aE Contact name (if it is logged as a Genesys contact)\u000d\u000aF\u000d\u000aDefines the queue through which the Interaction was routed / called\u000d\u000aG ACW Timer\u000d\u000aH Wrap-up code (select to define the type of call received)\u000d\u000aI\u000d\u000aAfter selecting a wrap-up code, you MUST ALWAYS select the Done button\u000d\u000aA\u000d\u000aC H\u000d\u000aI\u000d\u000aD\u000d\u000aE\u000d\u000aF\u000d\u000aB\u000d\u000aG","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 184\u000d\u000aCall Dashboard\u000d\u000aWhen answered, you will be able to manage the call using the dashboard located above the \u000d\u000ainteraction\u2019s details: \u000d\u000aTouch-Tone Dial Pad (click to toggle visibility)\u000d\u000aMute / Unmute\u000d\u000aHold\u000d\u000aTransfer\u000d\u000aConsult (Warm Transfer)\u000d\u000aConference (three, or more, parties in the call can speak to, and hear, one another)\u000d\u000aEnd Call","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 185\u000d\u000aCall Consults & Conferences\u000d\u000aThere are three ways to add parties to, or transfer, a call:\u000d\u000aTransfer (Cold Transfer)\u000d\u000aConsult (Warm Transfer)\u000d\u000aConference (three, or more, parties in the call \u000d\u000acan speak to, and hear, one another)\u000d\u000aDO NOT USE!\u000d\u000aIf every call were a hike, we would be \u000d\u000athe Guide. A cold transfer is like \u000d\u000aleaving an inexperienced hiker alone \u000d\u000aon a trail while the sun is setting. \u000d\u000aWe are responsible for leading our \u000d\u000acallers along the best path of care, \u000d\u000aeven when the terrain gets rocky. ","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 186\u000d\u000aStart a Consult\u000d\u000aInform the caller that they will be placed on Hold once you begin the consult. \u000d\u000a1. Select the Consult Icon:\u000d\u000a2. Enter the phone number you want to call.\u000d\u000a\u27a2 If calling a phone number, select the secondary Consult button to begin calling.\u000d\u000a\u27a2 If calling another Genesys user, or a contact in the address book, select the listing \u000d\u000ato start calling. \u000d\u000a\u27a2 The caller will be placed on hold automatically once the consult is initiated. ","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 187\u000d\u000a3. When your consulted contact answers the call, a new set of options will become \u000d\u000aavailable on your dashboard:\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Hold: This option will put your consulted contact on hold. You can manage your \u000d\u000ainitial caller on the original call dashboard.\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Transfer: This will transfer your caller to the consulted contact and disconnect \u000d\u000ayou from the call. \u000d\u000a\u27a2 Start Conference: All contacts in the call will be taken off of hold and be able to \u000d\u000aspeak to, and hear, one another. \u000d\u000ao Use this if more than three contacts need to participate in the call. \u000d\u000a\u27a2 Disconnect: This will disconnect the consulted contact from the call, but your \u000d\u000ainteraction with the original caller can continue. \u000d\u000ao This is DIFFERENT from the End Call button. \u000d\u000ao\u000d\u000aSelecting the red End Call button will disconnect all parties from the \u000d\u000ainteraction.\u000d\u000a4. Summarize the patient\u2019s concern, then use the Start Conference option.\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Selecting Start Conference will automatically take all parties off of hold.","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 188\u000d\u000a5. Select the Conference icon from the main Dashboard to view all parties in the call:\u000d\u000a6. When ready for transfer, disconnect yourself from the call. \u000d\u000a\u27a2 The call will continue with the remaining parties after you disconnect.\u000d\u000a7. Complete your after-call work (ACW) by selecting a wrap-up code and then Done.","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 189\u000d\u000aCheck Your Status\u000d\u000aAbout Status Selection\u000d\u000a\u2022 Determines an agent\u2019s eligibility to receive Calls and Interactions.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Manually adjusted to match current activity; does not sync with any other systems.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Agents do not need to adjust their status while connected to calls / interactions; the \u000d\u000asystem will automatically put them in a special Interacting status for the duration.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Supervisors use statuses to track users\u2019 availability and adherence to schedules.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Colored ring around profile picture corresponds with status:\u000d\u000a\u27a2 The ring around your profile will be Blue if you are On Queue or Interacting\u000d\u000a\u27a2 The ring around your profile will be Red if a Busy status is set. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Agents will see other users\u2019 statuses when attempting to call or transfer.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Some status options include secondary situational status options to better inform the \u000d\u000ateam of current activities. \u000d\u000aStatus Selection\u000d\u000aYou will choose your current status from your Profile icon:\u000d\u000a\u2022 Upon selection, a status will begin to display a timer. ","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 190\u000d\u000aStatus Key\u000d\u000aAvailable This will NOT allow the user to receive calls, but it does allow the user to \u000d\u000areceive internal calls within the organization. \u000d\u000a\u2022 This IS NOT the same as being On-Queue.\u000d\u000aAvailable auto-populates when you first log in but should be changed right \u000d\u000aaway. You should NEVER be in this status during your shift.\u000d\u000aAway Indicates nurse is not at their desk or is unavailable; all calls and transfers will \u000d\u000abe routed to voicemail.\u000d\u000aUse for restroom, water / coffee, DoorDash, etc.\u000d\u000a\u2022 No more than 20 minutes per shift IN TOTAL.\u000d\u000aBreak Used for breaks (2x15 min) per shift.\u000d\u000aMeal Used only for your lunch (30min).\u000d\u000aBusy Indicates nurse is not at their desk or is unavailable; all calls and transfers will \u000d\u000abe routed to voicemail.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Nurses should use extended ACW as needed to complete \u000d\u000adocumentation\u000d\u000aMeeting Coachings, Projects, etc\u2026\u000d\u000aTraining This should only be used as directed by a Team Lead or Supervisor.\u000d\u000aOn-Queue Indicates the user is available to take external calls for NN.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Selecting any other status will take the user Off-Queue\u000d\u000a\u2022 If switching Off-Queue using the toggle, the user will be placed in their \u000d\u000alast-used status. ","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 191\u000d\u000aSecondary Statuses\u000d\u000aPrimary statuses with a carrot icon (>) to the right have a Secondary Status.\u000d\u000a\u2022 For any Primary Status that include Secondary Status options, a Secondary Status must \u000d\u000abe selected to confirm your activity. \u000d\u000a\u2022 To return to the primary status list, click the primary status at the top. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Secondary statuses are division-aware; therefore, they may vary from team to team. \u000d\u000aStatuses & Locking Your System\u000d\u000aWhat happens when your system is locked while you are in the Available status?\u000d\u000a\u2022 Your status stays Available.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Internal calls continue to alert.\u000d\u000aWhat happens when your system is locked while you are On Queue?\u000d\u000a\u2022 You stay On Queue.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Calls and Interactions continue to alert.","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 192\u000d\u000aGoing On-Queue to Receive Calls\u000d\u000aYou can set yourself as On-Queue by two methods: \u000d\u000aMethod 1: Use the On / Off Queue Toggle beside your profile icon in the upper-right \u000d\u000acorner of the window. \u000d\u000aMethod 2: In the Agent Workspace screen within the Conversations pane. \u000d\u000a\u2022 It is recommended that you are already in the Agent Workspace when \u000d\u000agoing On-Queue as this is where you will be able to most effectively \u000d\u000amanage incoming calls, or dial out, as needed. ","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 193\u000d\u000aAfter Call Work (ACW) & Wrap-Up Codes\u000d\u000a\u2022 Agents are automatically placed into After Call Work (ACW) after a call ends. \u000d\u000a\u2022 Agents will not receive voice interactions from the queue while connected to ACW.\u000d\u000a\u2022 To exit ACW early and become eligible for waiting interactions, select a wrap-up code \u000d\u000aand click Done.\u000d\u000a\u2022 The timer indicates the amount of time an agent may stay connected to ACW; this varies \u000d\u000afrom queue-to-queue.\u000d\u000a \u000d\u000a911 Calls\u000d\u000a5 Minutes\u000d\u000aNon-911 Calls\u000d\u000a30 Seconds","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 194\u000d\u000aFailing to Answer an Interaction\u000d\u000aIf an incoming interaction / call is missed, you will be placed automatically into a unique Not \u000d\u000aResponding status and be ineligible to receive additional interactions until you manually go OnQueue. The notification proves two options; Make Eligible for Interactions (go on queue), and \u000d\u000aGo Off Queue. \u000d\u000aA Not Responding event may occur as the result of miss-clicking a Break or Meal status. \u000d\u000aEnsure the ring around your profile icon has changed to the correct status color before \u000d\u000alocking and departing from your system. ","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 195\u000d\u000aView Performance & Queue Activity\u000d\u000aThe options available to you in this menu will depend on your individual user permissions.\u000d\u000aTo view your individual performance data, or the activity of a particular queue:\u000d\u000a1. Open the Menu located in the upper-left corner of the Genesys \u000d\u000awindow. \u000d\u000a2. Select Analytics > Analytics Workspace","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 196\u000d\u000aThe Analytics Workspace opens as a tab within the Genesys window:\u000d\u000a\u2022 Selecting additional options in the Analytics Workspace will open additional tabs.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Select the three dots ( ) beside the tab\u2019s name to reload, close, or refresh it. \u000d\u000aMy Performance\u000d\u000aThe My Performance section of the Analytics Workspace includes the following options:\u000d\u000aMy Performance \u2022 View total interactions managed\u000d\u000a\u2022 Average interaction length\u000d\u000a\u2022 Average After Call Work (ACW)\u000d\u000aMy Interactions \u2022 View previous interactions (calls)\u000d\u000a\u2022 Listen to previous interactions\u000d\u000a\u2022 View ACW assigned to each interaction\u000d\u000aMy Queues Activity \u2022 Review current and historic interaction traffic of \u000d\u000aassigned queues. \u000d\u000aMy Status \u2022 See historic use of, and total time spent in, a status. \u000d\u000aTab management is key to \u000d\u000asuccessful navigation of the \u000d\u000aAnalytics Workspace. Genesys \u000d\u000awill remember your open \u000d\u000atabs between login sessions. ","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 197\u000d\u000aA Toggle the chart on / off\u000d\u000aB Click to select a date range \u000d\u000aC\u000d\u000aView Options\u000d\u000a\u2022 Refresh\u000d\u000a\u2022 Save View (to the main Analytics Space window)\u000d\u000a\u2022 Search \u000d\u000a\u2022 Filter\u000d\u000a\u2022 Export\u000d\u000a\u2022 Reset\u000d\u000aD Organize Columns\u000d\u000aA B C\u000d\u000aD\u000d\u000aYour Performance Metrics","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 198\u000d\u000aMy Queues Activity\u000d\u000a1. Queues that the agent is a member of are listed\u000d\u000a2. Real-time Metrics:\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Interactions\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Service level\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Agents on Queue\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Agent Status\u000d\u000a3. Metrics can be added / removed using the (+) option to the right of the column listings. \u000d\u000aMy Interactions\u000d\u000aEach line represents an individual interaction. Click the interaction to view the call\u2019s recording. \u000d\u000aA Set the Filter by Media option to All\u000d\u000aB\u000d\u000aClick the three dots ( ) on the right side of each \u000d\u000ainteraction to copy the Conversation ID \u000d\u000aA\u000d\u000aB","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 199\u000d\u000aCommon Errors\u000d\u000aLogging In\u000d\u000a\u2022 If the agent receives an error: \u000d\u000aSorry, there is a Problem with the Organization You Provided\u000d\u000a\u2014there are two possible explanations:\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Wrong Region (US East/US West)\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Typo or space in Organization\u2019s name\u000d\u000a\u2022 If the agent says their email address and password are not working, there are two \u000d\u000apossible explanations:\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Have not activated their account and set a password.\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Trying to log in using email / password when configured for SSO\u000d\u000a\u2022 Trying to log in on the wrong screen (must be on the purple panel for SSO)\u000d\u000aNo Phone Selected\u000d\u000aAgents with a red phone will not be able to make or receive calls or interactions; three common \u000d\u000aRed Phone issues:\u000d\u000a\u2022 Select a phone to make / receive phone calls\u000d\u000a\u2022 Your browser does not have permission to access your microphone. \u000d\u000a\u2022 You have a WebRTC phone selected, but Genesys Cloud is unable to connect to a \u000d\u000acompatible microphone.\u000d\u000aA selected phone is \u000d\u000anecessary to make \u000d\u000aoutbound calls and receive \u000d\u000aincoming interactions in \u000d\u000aGenesys. ","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 200\u000d\u000aSelect a Phone\u000d\u000a1. Click your profile icon in the upper-right corner.\u000d\u000a2. Search for, and select, your assigned phone:\u000d\u000aCheck Windows Sound Settings\u000d\u000aIf your system or browser does not recognize a microphone, or if the microphone assigned \u000d\u000athrough Preferences is disconnected, Genesys may be unable to make calls:\u000d\u000a\u2022 Double-check your system\u2019s Sound Settings.\u000d\u000a\u27a2\u000d\u000aAccess your system\u2019s settings menu through the Windows / Start icon ( )\u000d\u000a\u27a2 Check input settings.\u000d\u000aMy_Phone_Ex\u000d\u000aMy_Phone_Example","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 201\u000d\u000a\u2022 Double-check your Preferences settings in Genesys.\u000d\u000a\u2022\u000d\u000aIn your web browser, select the ( ) icon of your address bar and allow permissions for \u000d\u000ayour preferred microphone.","CAD-to-CAD\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 202\u000d\u000aOverview\u000d\u000a1. 911 / Field gets an NTL eligible call\u000d\u000a2. 911 / Field provides details to their CAD\u000d\u000a3. Their CAD contacts our CAD to check for an available nurse in Logis\u000d\u000ao If no nurse is available in Logis, the incident is not sent to 911 Nurse Navigation, \u000d\u000aand contract sends resources to patient.\u000d\u000a4. The available nurse is provided the incident \u000d\u000a5. The available nurse receives the associated call\u000d\u000aStatus Management\u000d\u000aBecause CAD-to-CAD checks your status in Logis to see if you are available for a call, accurate \u000d\u000astatus management is key to the successful operation of NN. \u000d\u000aIf you\u2019re not ready to take a call, you should \u000d\u000abe \u201cBusy\u201d or \u201cUnavailable\u201d in Logis.\u000d\u000aWhen the system says we\u2019re available, but we don\u2019t pick up the phone:\u000d\u000a\u2022 Contracts blows up our phones and our abandoned calls increase.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Call Takers and Field Staff lose faith in our program.\u000d\u000aIt\u2019s easy to fix staffing, BUT It\u2019s hard to repair lost faith","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 203\u000d\u000aMatching Statuses \u000d\u000a\u2022 Contracts see the system is working as designed.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Reports of \u201cNo nurse available\u201d from our partners are monitored by leadership and \u000d\u000awe look into the cause (number of staff on shift, staff in Aux, etc\u2026), and we work \u000d\u000atowards a solution internally.\u000d\u000aKeys to Success\u000d\u000aAdjust your Logis Window Proportions\u000d\u000aThe Logis Availability window can be stretched and resized to match your \u000d\u000aeconomy.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Hover your mouse curser on the window\u2019s edge to stretch it to the \u000d\u000adesired size.\u000d\u000a\u2022 Keep it near your Genesys window\u000d\u000aPosition your Logis Window\u000d\u000aLogis Availability stays on top of all other programs. You can even put it over \u000d\u000ayour Genesys window which we have found to encourage the fastest system \u000d\u000anavigation.\u000d\u000aUpdate Logis for Live Calls\u000d\u000aWhen you answer a call in Genesys, immediately click \u201cBusy\u201d in Logis.\u000d\u000aSet Your Availability in Logis\u000d\u000aWhen you switch back to \u201cOn Queue\u201d in Genesys, immediately mark \u000d\u000ayourself \u201cAvailable\u201d in Logis.","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 204\u000d\u000aWindow Adjustment\u000d\u000a \u000d\u000aWide-Width Window Adjustment\u000d\u000aNarrow Window Adjustment Window Placed Over Genesys","Logis\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 205\u000d\u000aOverview\u000d\u000aA. Search the patient\u2019s name here. Verify their address\u000d\u000aB. Provide the contract name here\u000d\u000aC. Enter the patient\u2019s phone number\u000d\u000aD. Caller Name and relationship to patient\u000d\u000aE. Input the patient\u2019s address and include their apartment / building / unit number and \u000d\u000agate code (if applicable) \u000d\u000aF. Enter the patient\u2019s insurance type to see the dispositions\u000d\u000aG. Tag the call as 911 Call Center, AMR Field, Fire Field\u000d\u000aH. Reference Incident / Call for Service Reference Number \u000d\u000aA B\u000d\u000aF\u000d\u000aE\u000d\u000aC\u000d\u000aD\u000d\u000aG\u000d\u000aH","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 206\u000d\u000a \u000d\u000a ","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 207\u000d\u000aCan\u2019t Find the Patient?\u000d\u000aEnter the patient\u2019s demographics here to create a new patient, if not found.","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 208\u000d\u000aSix Required fields\u000d\u000a1 First Name 2 Last Name\u000d\u000a3 Date of Birth (DOB) 4\u000d\u000aGender\u000d\u000a5 Phone Number 6 Address\u000d\u000aUse dashes Include apt / building / unit number\u000d\u000aInsurance type is required only for DCFEMS and Riverside contracts","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 209\u000d\u000aBeing Evaluated\u000d\u000a\u2022 After you open your CAD-to-CAD call on the right side, click the Being Evaluated button \u000d\u000a(bottom left) so that your team will know you are working the call.\u000d\u000a\u27a2 If not CAD-to-CAD, enter patient information and click Save before clicking Being \u000d\u000aEvaluated to claim the call on the incident list.\u000d\u000aVisit the Quality Assurance segment of this guide \u2605\u2605\u2605\u2605\u2605 to review specific QA evaluation guidelines. ","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 210\u000d\u000aScheduling in Gantt\u000d\u000aSchedule follow-up calls for the next business day\u000d\u000aEdit the pickup location to \u201chome\u201d\u000d\u000aChange the time to reflect 10:00 AM in the patient\u2019s time zone","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 211\u000d\u000aSchedule Follow-Up Calls\u000d\u000a1. Select the Lock icon to open and edit fields:\u000d\u000a2. Under the Pickup section, click the address field and delete the address listed.\u000d\u000a3. Type \u2018Home\u2019 and select 4400 TX-121 Lewisville, TX \u000d\u000a\u27a2 It is the first in the dropdown list","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 212\u000d\u000a4. Edit the date and time to reflect 10:00 AM in the patient\u2019s time zone on the following\u000d\u000abusiness day.\u000d\u000a5. Click Save and exit.","Crisp DC\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 213\u000d\u000aOverview\u000d\u000a\u2022 Nurses will use Crisp DC to verify pt insurance and identify pt\u2019s \u2018home\u2019 clinic\u000d\u000a\u2022 You will receive an email to set up your CRISP account. \u000d\u000a\u27a2 The set-up email is only good for 72 hours.\u000d\u000a\u27a2 You must log into your CRISP account at least monthly to maintain your access\u000d\u000a\u2022 For documentation guidelines in Logis, carefully review the DC FEMS Contract.\u000d\u000a\u2022 While it is not required for a patient to have insurance to receive our services, it is \u000d\u000aimportant attempt to get this information\u000d\u000a\u27a2 DCFEMS tracks this data to use for reimbursements from insurance providers\u000d\u000aLogin\u000d\u000aLink: \ud83d\udd17Open DC Crisp\u000d\u000aPatient Search\u000d\u000a\u2022 Enter the patient\u2019s first name, last name, and DOB to start your search. Results are \u000d\u000adisplayed to the right of the search menu","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 214\u000d\u000a\u2022 Search results include first name, last name, DOB, gender, address, and match score:\u000d\u000a\u2022 Select the patient you wish to view\u000d\u000a\u2022 From the app selection menu, choose Snapshot\u000d\u000a\u2022 You will be asked to verify why you are viewing the patient\u2019s data. \u000d\u000a\u27a2 Select Care Coordination","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 215\u000d\u000aSnapshot\u000d\u000a\u2022 Find the Medicaid ID in Patient Demographics:\u000d\u000a\u2022 Encounters from A1T keeps a list of the patient\u2019s most recent clinic / hospital visits\u000d\u000a\u2022 Prioritize sending the patient to the most recently visited clinic\u000d\u000a\u2022 If uninsured or no insurance, Unity Clinics have on-site enrollment","DC Taxi\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 216\u000d\u000aLogin \u000d\u000aLink: \ud83d\udd17Open DC Taxi\u000d\u000a \u000d\u000aCorp Account / Customer\u000d\u000a911\u000d\u000aUser Number\u000d\u000a1\u000d\u000aPIN\u000d\u000a1234","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 217\u000d\u000aReserve a Ride\u000d\u000a1. Delete the pre-existing information auto-prepopulated in each field. \u000d\u000a2. Enter the patient\u2019s name under Name.\u000d\u000a3. Enter the patient\u2019s phone number twice\u000d\u000a\u27a2 In the Phone field\u000d\u000a\u27a2 In the Phone Notifications box","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 218\u000d\u000aPick Up\u000d\u000a4. Date / time: Enter the date and time for right now or you can pre-schedule the ride for \u000d\u000anext day. \u000d\u000a5. Enter the address where patient needs to be picked up at.","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 219\u000d\u000aOptions\u000d\u000a6. Comments can be:\u000d\u000a\u27a2 \u201cPlease call patient upon arrival\u201d \u000d\u000a\u27a2 \u201cPatient is elderly and will need time to get to the vehicle\u201d\u000d\u000a\u27a2 \u2026anything that is important.\u000d\u000a7. If the patient needs a van, select Wheelchair.","System Applications 911 Nurse Navigation Job Training & Reference Materials \u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 220\u000d\u000aCustomer Requirements\u000d\u000a8. Auth Code: Enter Logis Incident Number \u000d\u000aRequestor: Your name\u000d\u000aDestinations\u000d\u000a9. Enter the address the patient is going to. \u000d\u000a10. Click \u201cBook a Trip\u201d.","Recognition\u000d\u000aLast Published: October 2, 2026 Page 221\u000d\u000aWe are working hard to bring you the all-new Recognition section! \u000d\u000aThank you for your patience. "]